{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EkGDo1ezG16Jj3N86SuPMS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"TrackMania 2003 original Nadeo game modes Race Puzzle Survival coppers environments Desert Rally Snow\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"TrackMania (2003 video game)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TrackMania_(2003_video_game)\"},{\"title\":\"TrackMania (2003 video game)\",\"url\":\"https://wikipedia.com/wiki/TrackMania_Original\"},{\"title\":\"TrackMania (2003 video game)\",\"url\":\"https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/TrackMania_(2003_video_game)\"},{\"title\":\"bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io\",\"url\":\"https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/TrackMania.html\"},{\"title\":\"giantbomb.com\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/TrackMania\"},{\"title\":\"www.giantbomb.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-8972/\"},{\"title\":\"giantbomb.com\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/trackmania/3030-8972/\"},{\"title\":\"www.giantbomb.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/wd/3030-8972\"},{\"title\":\"TrackMania (2003 video game)\",\"url\":\"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/TrackMania_(2003_video_game)\"},{\"title\":\"Nadeo Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://nadeo.fandom.com/wiki/TrackMania_Original\"},{\"title\":\"Games Encyclopedia Top Games PC PS4 PS3 Xbox One Xbox 360 Switch Android iOS Rankings Images Companies\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamepressure.com/games/trackmania/z5d89\"},{\"title\":\"www.tweaktown.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.tweaktown.com/gaming/2277/trackmania_sunrise_pc_review/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Loading AI tools\",\"url\":\"https://wikiwand.com/en/articles/TrackMania\"},{\"title\":\"Trackmania United PC Review\",\"url\":\"https://www.tweaktown.com/gaming/2521/trackmania_united_pc_review/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"the official trackmania united thread.161922\",\"url\":\"https://neogaf.com/threads/the-official-trackmania-united-thread.161922/\"},{\"title\":\"TrackMania PC Review\",\"url\":\"https://www.tweaktown.com/gaming/2072/trackmania_pc_review/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"This article is a stub. You can help Codex Gamicus by expanding it. |\",\"url\":\"https://gamicus.fandom.com/wiki/TrackMania_DS\"},{\"title\":\"Trackmania Nations\",\"url\":\"https://extension.wikiwand.com/en/Trackmania_Nations\"}]\n\nThe search confirms the core of your question, with one naming discrepancy to note.\n\n- **Modes:** The 2003 original had three solo modes, Race, Puzzle, and Survival, with an equal number of tracks per environment. There are also three modes: Race, Puzzle, and Survival, each of which features an equal number of tracks for each environment. Survival was dropped from later games. The \"Survival\" mode does not appear in the later games.\n- **Environments:** Sources agree on Desert, Rally, and Snow. One mirror says there are three environments to choose from: Rally, Snow, and Desert, each of which offers a unique car. A Giant Bomb page lists Desert among its environments (index 6-2), and another source describes the original as offering Desert, countryside, and snow.\n- **Naming discrepancy:** The Nadeo Wiki names the three environments Alpine, Speed, and Rally, but attributes that list to TrackMania Original, the 2005 re-release. It says that version includes the three original environments, Alpine, Speed and Rally. So the Desert/Rally/Snow names come from the 2003 original, while Alpine/Speed/Rally are the 2005 names.\n- **Coppers:** Coppers are the in-game currency. Players had to purchase pieces (called \"bricks\") by spending an in-game currency called coppers which was attained by completing the various pre-made tracks for a bronze, silver or gold medal.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"577815c2-c5b9-4aab-a82c-31ac9d89687a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:11.578Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"TrackMania 2003 original Nadeo game modes Race Puzzle Survival coppers environments Desert Rally Snow","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01MVsZznNbEPHT4A3v2xwobo","content":[{"title":"TrackMania (2003 video game)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TrackMania_(2003_video_game)"},{"title":"TrackMania (2003 video game)","url":"https://wikipedia.com/wiki/TrackMania_Original"},{"title":"TrackMania (2003 video game)","url":"https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/TrackMania_(2003_video_game)"},{"title":"bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io","url":"https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/TrackMania.html"},{"title":"giantbomb.com","url":"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/TrackMania"},{"title":"www.giantbomb.com","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-8972/"},{"title":"giantbomb.com","url":"https://giantbomb.com/trackmania/3030-8972/"},{"title":"www.giantbomb.com","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/wd/3030-8972"},{"title":"TrackMania (2003 video game)","url":"https://ipfs.ssi.eecc.de/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/TrackMania_(2003_video_game)"},{"title":"Nadeo Wiki","url":"https://nadeo.fandom.com/wiki/TrackMania_Original"},{"title":"Games Encyclopedia Top Games PC PS4 PS3 Xbox One Xbox 360 Switch Android iOS Rankings Images Companies","url":"https://www.gamepressure.com/games/trackmania/z5d89"},{"title":"www.tweaktown.com","url":"https://www.tweaktown.com/gaming/2277/trackmania_sunrise_pc_review/index.html"},{"title":"Loading AI tools","url":"https://wikiwand.com/en/articles/TrackMania"},{"title":"Trackmania United PC Review","url":"https://www.tweaktown.com/gaming/2521/trackmania_united_pc_review/index.html"},{"title":"the official trackmania united thread.161922","url":"https://neogaf.com/threads/the-official-trackmania-united-thread.161922/"},{"title":"TrackMania PC Review","url":"https://www.tweaktown.com/gaming/2072/trackmania_pc_review/index.html"},{"title":"This article is a stub. You can help Codex Gamicus by expanding it. |","url":"https://gamicus.fandom.com/wiki/TrackMania_DS"},{"title":"Trackmania Nations","url":"https://extension.wikiwand.com/en/Trackmania_Nations"}]},"The search confirms the core of your question, with one naming discrepancy to note.\n\n- **Modes:** The 2003 original had three solo modes, Race, Puzzle, and Survival, with an equal number of tracks per environment. There are also three modes: Race, Puzzle, and Survival, each of which features an equal number of tracks for each environment. Survival was dropped from later games. The \"Survival\" mode does not appear in the later games.\n- **Environments:** Sources agree on Desert, Rally, and Snow. One mirror says there are three environments to choose from: Rally, Snow, and Desert, each of which offers a unique car. A Giant Bomb page lists Desert among its environments (index 6-2), and another source describes the original as offering Desert, countryside, and snow.\n- **Naming discrepancy:** The Nadeo Wiki names the three environments Alpine, Speed, and Rally, but attributes that list to TrackMania Original, the 2005 re-release. It says that version includes the three original environments, Alpine, Speed and Rally. So the Desert/Rally/Snow names come from the 2003 original, while Alpine/Speed/Rally are the 2005 names.\n- **Coppers:** Coppers are the in-game currency. Players had to purchase pieces (called \"bricks\") by spending an in-game currency called coppers which was attained by completing the various pre-made tracks for a bronze, silver or gold medal."],"durationSeconds":7.245464035999991,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EkGDo1ezG16Jj3N86SuPMS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q7oxCdzbGzg5DPXULr6GRL","type":"tool_result","content":"**TrackMania (2003)** is a racing and puzzle game developed by Nadeo, the first title in the series.\n\n**Gameplay**\n- **Currency:** Players earn \"coppers\" by racing pre-built tracks, then spend them on building blocks.\n- **Blocks:** Options include regular roads, checkpoints, long bends, loop-the-loops, and jumps. Blocks snap to a grid, and most connect automatically when placed next to each other. Roads can be dragged to form straight sections and 90-degree corners.\n- **Environments:** Rally (Countryside), Snow (Alpine), and Desert (Speed), each with its own car and handling.\n- **Modes:** Race, Puzzle, and Survival, with an equal number of tracks per environment. The page notes Survival does not appear in later games.\n- **Cars:** Three styles (rally super minis, alpine 4x4s, and speed muscle cars), with skins for a total of 87 cars. Players can paint skins with the built-in car painter or an external graphics editor.\n- **Multiplayer:** Hotseat, LAN, and Internet play. Players can upload tracks or skins to the game's website for others to use.\n\n**Release and credits**\n- **Developer:** Nadeo\n- **Publishers:** Focus Home Interactive (France), Digital Jesters (UK), Enlight Software (US)\n- **Director:** Florent Castelnérac\n- **Composer:** Henri-Pierre Pellegrin\n- **Platform:** Windows\n- **Release:** November 21, 2003 (France), November 28, 2003 (UK), June 24, 2004 (North America)\n\n**Reception**\n- Metacritic aggregate: 74/100, described as \"average\" reviews.\n- GameSpot (8/10) called it \"completely worth it\" for fans of PC driving games.\n- GameSpy (3/5) found the races \"fast-paced and reasonably fun\" but \"often too easy.\"\n- IGN (5.9/10) called it \"a temporary diversion.\"\n- GameSpot named it the best computer game of July 2004.\n\n**TrackMania Original (2005)**\nA re-release on October 12, 2005, running on the TrackMania Sunrise engine. It added over 10 block types and the ability to import 3D car models.\n\n**Not covered in the source:** The page does not mention medals, ghosts, replays, or the original game's engine."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"3194c19a-1228-42d4-a8c1-04bdc5112dd0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:14.159Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":146908,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**TrackMania (2003)** is a racing and puzzle game developed by Nadeo, the first title in the series.\n\n**Gameplay**\n- **Currency:** Players earn \"coppers\" by racing pre-built tracks, then spend them on building blocks.\n- **Blocks:** Options include regular roads, checkpoints, long bends, loop-the-loops, and jumps. Blocks snap to a grid, and most connect automatically when placed next to each other. Roads can be dragged to form straight sections and 90-degree corners.\n- **Environments:** Rally (Countryside), Snow (Alpine), and Desert (Speed), each with its own car and handling.\n- **Modes:** Race, Puzzle, and Survival, with an equal number of tracks per environment. The page notes Survival does not appear in later games.\n- **Cars:** Three styles (rally super minis, alpine 4x4s, and speed muscle cars), with skins for a total of 87 cars. Players can paint skins with the built-in car painter or an external graphics editor.\n- **Multiplayer:** Hotseat, LAN, and Internet play. Players can upload tracks or skins to the game's website for others to use.\n\n**Release and credits**\n- **Developer:** Nadeo\n- **Publishers:** Focus Home Interactive (France), Digital Jesters (UK), Enlight Software (US)\n- **Director:** Florent Castelnérac\n- **Composer:** Henri-Pierre Pellegrin\n- **Platform:** Windows\n- **Release:** November 21, 2003 (France), November 28, 2003 (UK), June 24, 2004 (North America)\n\n**Reception**\n- Metacritic aggregate: 74/100, described as \"average\" reviews.\n- GameSpot (8/10) called it \"completely worth it\" for fans of PC driving games.\n- GameSpy (3/5) found the races \"fast-paced and reasonably fun\" but \"often too easy.\"\n- IGN (5.9/10) called it \"a temporary diversion.\"\n- GameSpot named it the best computer game of July 2004.\n\n**TrackMania Original (2005)**\nA re-release on October 12, 2005, running on the TrackMania Sunrise engine. It added over 10 block types and the ability to import 3D car models.\n\n**Not covered in the source:** The page does not mention medals, ghosts, replays, or the original game's engine.","durationMs":8472,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TrackMania_(2003_video_game)"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Q7oxCdzbGzg5DPXULr6GRL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
