{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015LjnQwyG4yK6ie5NheGXPq","type":"tool_result","content":"/* =============================================================================\n * 7. CAMERA  world.camera: every camera a real 3D one, its pose worked out in the game's fixed steps (so the controls\n *    that read it play back the same), its picture placed when the world draws.\n *      'view'   the 2D engine's views as 3D cameras following the target (camera.target: the first hero unless set), a\n *               little ahead of its aim with the 2D camera's lag: game.view (V cycles it), game.yaw ([ ] turn it),\n *               game.zoom (the wheel, a pinch, Settings: Camera zoom). proj 'persp' (a lens, camera.fov) or 'ortho'\n *               (the 2D engine's flat projection); dist pulls it back. Walls between the level and the camera are cut\n *               low, pillars between it and the target cut to stumps (camera.cut false keeps them)\n *      'chase'  behind the target and above it: it swings round behind as the target moves (chase.auto), turns with\n *               [ ], the mouse once a click captures it (Esc frees it); game.zoom pulls it in; it slides in front of\n *               walls rather than through them\n *      'first'  the target's eyes (its body isn't drawn), 'fly' a free camera the move stick flies (jump up, dash\n *               down), 'fixed' stays where camera.fixed says ({ x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }): a game that runs its\n *               own camera (a shooter's eyes, its over-the-shoulder view) sets it every step\n *      'zones'  Resident Evil's: the region the target is in gives the camera (camera.zones: a fixed one, one that turns\n *               to follow, one that slides on a rail), a cut when it moves on, held back until it is `margin` units\n *               into the next region (hysteresis: no flicking back and forth on a border)\n *    camera.ground(move) -> the move stick turned to the ground ([x, y], W walks away from the camera); across a cut it\n *    keeps the old camera's way while the stick is held the same way (no walking back out of a doorway);\n *    camera.steer(actor, move, dt) -> the same, or tank controls (the player's setting: World3D.CONTROLS);\n *    camera.lock(from, target | list) -> lock-on (Zelda's targeting): the chase and first cameras turn to frame both,\n *    ground() strafes round the target, a reticle marks it; cycle(list) the next in sight, unlock();\n *    camera.aim(actor) -> the angle the mouse (on the floor) or right stick points from it, or null;\n *    camera.heading: the ground angle it looks along; camera.pose: { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, fov, ortho } now\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst headingOf = yawDeg => Math.atan2(-Math.cos(yawDeg * DEG), -Math.sin(yawDeg * DEG));\nconst engineYaw = a => ((Math.round(Math.atan2(-Math.cos(a), -Math.sin(a)) / DEG) % 360) + 360) % 360;\nclass Camera3D {\n  /** made by the world: new E.World3D(game, { camera: { mode, proj, fov, dist, lag, lead, chase, first } }) */\n  constructor(world, o = {}) {\n6:its exact fixed steps, scenes, input, pause menu, settings, touch buttons, sound, the rigs and their moves, the HUD. This\n35:- Deterministic: the world steps in the game's fixed steps; gameplay randomness comes from E.rng(seed); the camera's\n128:  world.block({ x, y, z, w, d, h, yaw } | { x, y, z, r, h }): an invisible fixed collider (walls you draw your own way;\n135:hero: a kinematic capsule walked by Rapier's character controller: it slides along walls, climbs stairs and slopes,\n155:  world.box({ x, y, z, w, d, h, color, side, fixed, mass }); a prop has x, y, z, q (its rotation), data\n172:  world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll).box(x, y, z, w, d, h, color).ball(x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, color).tube(x0, y0, z0, x1,\n186:  turn it), 'first' (the target's eyes), 'fly', 'fixed' (camera.fixed = { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }: your own),\n187:  'zones' (Resident Evil's: camera.zones = [{ box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], at: [x, y, z], look: [x, y, z] (fixed) | follow:\n216:Rapier rolls (walls, bumps, ramps, jumps) steered by E.Car's arcade handling; an actor. Each step v.update(dt, null,\n228:window across it) }): each step f.update(dt, { steer: [x, y], boost, brake, roll: -1 | 1 (a barrel roll: f.rolling),\n229:loop }); f.x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, speed, frame (the rail's point), hitGround; f.seek(list, { cone, range }): what a\n230:charged shot locks on; f.at(): where to draw it this frame. world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll) tips the pen.\n232:height, ahead, lag, fov, roll }): a kart's camera, a ship's (follow f.frame on a rail).\n237:camera 'fixed' with capture: each step turn by camera.takeMouse(), set camera.fixed (the eyes, or over the shoulder pulled\n259:runs fixed steps at once; game.input.hold / tap script input. The kits expose window.__game.\n293:const HERO_QUERY = ig(4, 1 | 2 | 64);   // a hero's controller steers round the level, props and platforms; its capsule shoves monsters\n611:  /** Rapier's fixed colliders for all of it, into a new physics world */\n613:    const fixed = pw.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.fixed());\n614:    const box = (x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, g = GROUPS.level) => pw.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.cuboid((x1 - x0) / 2, (y1 - y0) / 2, (z1 - z0) / 2).setTranslation((x0 + x1) / 2, (y0 + y1) / 2,\n615:    const hull = pts => pw.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.convexHull(new Float32Array(pts.flat())).setFriction(.6).setCollisionGroups(GROUPS.level), fixed);\n627:    for (const t of this.torches) pw.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.cylinder(6, 5).setRotation(Z_UP).setTranslation(t.x, t.y, t.z + 6).setCollisionGroups(GROUPS.level), fixed);\n974:    const b = pw.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.fixed().setTranslation((cx + .5) * this.cs, (cy + .5) * this.cs, 0).setRotation(Z_UP));\n1182:/** a frame's turn as a 3 x 3 matrix in engine axes (rows x, y, z): yaw about z, then pitch (the nose up), then roll (the\n1184:function frameOf(yaw, pitch, roll) {\n1185:  const cy = Math.cos(yaw), sy = Math.sin(yaw), cp = Math.cos(pitch), sp = Math.sin(pitch), cr = Math.cos(roll), sr = Math.sin(roll);\n1186:  const f = [cy * cp, sy * cp, sp], r0 = [-sy, cy, 0], u0 = [-cy * sp, -sy * sp, cp];   // forward; right and up before the roll\n1203:   *  (the nose up, about its y) and roll (its right side down, about its x): a car on a slope, a ship in a turn; returns\n1205:  at(x = 0, y = 0, z = 0, yaw = 0, k = 1, pitch = 0, roll = 0) {\n1207:    this.M = pitch || roll ? frameOf(yaw, pitch, roll) : null; return this;\n1317: *     so a new kind or placement builds no shader. A solid one gets a fixed collider from the box the 2D engine collides\n1536:/* ---- cards: the engine's own drawings in atlas pages (fixed 512+ pixel canvases, each its own texture and instanced\n1612: * 7. CAMERA  world.camera: every camera a real 3D one, its pose worked out in the game's fixed steps (so the controls\n1623: *               down), 'fixed' stays where camera.fixed says ({ x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }): a game that runs its\n1625: *      'zones'  Resident Evil's: the region the target is in gives the camera (camera.zones: a fixed one, one that turns\n1641:    /** mode: 'view' | 'chase' | 'first' | 'fly' | 'fixed'; proj: 'persp' | 'ortho' (view mode); fov: the view lens\n1647:     *  round behind the target as it moves) }; first: { pitch, fov }; fly: { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, fov }; fixed: a pose */\n1651:     *  fast it swings after the target's heading), fov (64), roll (0: the share of a flyer's roll it takes) } */\n1652:    this.behind = Object.assign({ dist: 70, height: 24, ahead: 40, lag: 5, fov: 64, roll: 0 }, o.behind);\n1653:    this.fly = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 90, yaw: -Math.PI / 2, pitch: -.32, fov: 70 }; this.fixed = o.fixed || null;\n1659:     *  (camera.takeMouse()) instead of turning the camera: a shooter turns its own (fixed) camera */\n1662:     *  fixed one looks), follow: true (it turns to follow the target), rail: [[x, y, z], [x, y, z]] (it slides along the\n1678:    if (!['view', 'chase', 'first', 'fly', 'fixed', 'zones', 'behind'].includes(mode) || mode === this.mode) return this;\n1683:    if (mode === 'fixed' && !this.fixed && p) this.fixed = { x: p.x, y: p.y, z: p.z, yaw: p.yaw, pitch: p.pitch, fov: p.fov || 60 };\n1685:    if ((mode === 'view' || mode === 'fixed') && !this.capture && typeof document !== 'undefined' && document.pointerLockElement) { document.exitPointerLock(); this.locked = false; }\n1697:  /** a step of the game: where every camera is (fixed steps: the controls read it) */\n1706:    this.pose = P ? this._passPose(P) : m === 'view' ? this._viewPose(dt, t) : m === 'chase' ? this._chasePose(dt, t) : m === 'first' ? this._firstPose(dt, t) : m === 'fly' ? this._flyPose(dt) : \n1745:    s[3] += E.angDiff(s[3], yaw) * k; s[4] += E.angDiff(s[4], pitch) * k; s[5] += ((t.roll || 0) * B.roll - s[5]) * k;\n1751:    return { x, y, z, yaw: Math.atan2(dy, dx), pitch: Math.atan2(look[2] - z, Math.hypot(dx, dy)), roll: s[5], fov: B.fov, ortho: false };\n1871:    if (p.roll) cam.rotateZ(p.roll);   // (a fixed pose may lean: a slide, a wall run)\n1900: * 8. ACTORS  world.hero(o): a kinematic capsule that Rapier's character controller walks (it slides along walls,\n1957: * 8b. VEHICLES AND FLYERS  world.vehicle(o): a kart, a car or a hovercraft, a ball that Rapier rolls (walls, bumps,\n1960: *     drives an E.Car. world.flyer(o): a ship's arcade flight (yaw, pitch, a bank, barrel rolls and loops, boost and\n1977:     *  onGround; airT; bumped (it hit something this step); tilt: [pitch, roll] it is drawn at (the ground's slope) */\n2060:     *  bank (.8: the roll into a turn), invert (up dives), low (14: its least height over the ground), bounds: [x0, y0,\n2062:     *  about a window w x h across it) }; x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll: where it is and its turn; speed; rolling (seconds\n2063:     *  of a barrel roll left: turn shots aside with it), looping; frame: the rail's point ({ x, y, z, yaw, pitch }: the\n2066:    Object.assign(this, { world, x: o.x || 0, y: o.y || 0, z: o.z ?? 120, yaw: o.yaw || 0, pitch: 0, roll: 0, speed: this.o.speed, rolling: 0, rollDir: 1, looping: 0, frame: null, d: 0, ox: 0, oy\n2073:  /** one step (before world.step): an intent { steer: [x, y] (the stick: x right, y down), boost, brake, roll (-1 | 1:\n2074:   *  a barrel roll that way), loop (a loop: free flight) } */\n2076:    (this._ip || (this._ip = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0])).splice(0, 6, this.x, this.y, this.z, this.yaw, this.pitch, this.roll);   // (where it was: a frame between steps draws it part way)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"6afe43a2-7bd1-4d07-8589-828c18fb2ed2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:48.779Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/* =============================================================================\n * 7. CAMERA  world.camera: every camera a real 3D one, its pose worked out in the game's fixed steps (so the controls\n *    that read it play back the same), its picture placed when the world draws.\n *      'view'   the 2D engine's views as 3D cameras following the target (camera.target: the first hero unless set), a\n *               little ahead of its aim with the 2D camera's lag: game.view (V cycles it), game.yaw ([ ] turn it),\n *               game.zoom (the wheel, a pinch, Settings: Camera zoom). proj 'persp' (a lens, camera.fov) or 'ortho'\n *               (the 2D engine's flat projection); dist pulls it back. Walls between the level and the camera are cut\n *               low, pillars between it and the target cut to stumps (camera.cut false keeps them)\n *      'chase'  behind the target and above it: it swings round behind as the target moves (chase.