{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyijBS67C4PY2oy26EB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BUZs5sFbUuAcamUmuRt9GK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/crackmania-plan-research-xbd1c73/engine/dist/handoff && grep -n -i \"symbol\\|glyph\\|buttonStyle\\|padStyle\" API-INDEX.md | head -20; echo ----; grep -n -i \"attract\" API-INDEX.md | head -20","description":"Search the API index for button glyphs and attract mode"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1673,"cache_read_input_tokens":184718,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1673},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"21a911c3-2f9c-48ee-9908-1eaf9a65ae49","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:57:27.104Z","request_id":"req_011CggyiiuJZcTaYNxydzvkN","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BUZs5sFbUuAcamUmuRt9GK":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/crackmania-plan-research-xbd1c73/engine/dist/handoff && grep -n -i \"symbol\\|glyph\\|buttonStyle\\|padStyle\" API-INDEX.md | head -20; echo ----; grep -n -i \"attract\" API-INDEX.md | head -20","description":"Search the API index for button glyphs and attract mode"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BUZs5sFbUuAcamUmuRt9GK","type":"tool_result","content":"283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n----\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a number (seconds), nothing (one step), a condition (a function, or E.until(fn)), a tween or script (until it is done), a generator (run as a script of its own, and waited for), E.all([...]) or E.any([...]) (each of these). It runs at once to its first yield. Cutscenes, boss patterns, wave timelines, tutorials, attract modes. Returns the Script\n1220:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1233:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n1234:- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n1238:- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1251:- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"a92e4df2-48a4-4f57-901d-2cb64e3457e5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:57:27.124Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's