{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2xJ9mNaXxWSUv481GQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CBkS32eHVqusKDaomcgJx2","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work/PLAN.md","offset":509,"limit":240},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10109,"cache_read_input_tokens":494989,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10109},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"aba52242-72a3-4a92-a66a-3547dd6e1392","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:39:24.175Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2xHuPyiudbAM2ydwRJ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CBkS32eHVqusKDaomcgJx2":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work/PLAN.md","offset":509,"limit":240}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CBkS32eHVqusKDaomcgJx2","type":"tool_result","content":"509\t     coast: if gas = 0: a −= v̂·1.2 m/s²;  rolling: a −= v̂·surface.roll;  aero: a −= v·cd·|v|\n510\t     boost: if boostT > 0: a += f·CFG.boostAccel; boostT −= dt\n511\t     steering (bicycle model): δmax = lerp(δlo, δhi, clamp(|s|/vtop, 0, 1)^0.7)\n512\t       steerIn: keyboard input ramps to ±1 over 0.12 s and back over 0.08 s; sticks apply directly (deadzone by engine)\n513\t       drift = brake > 0.5 && |steer| > 0.5 && s > 60 km/h (TrackMania's brake-drift)\n514\t       yawRate = s·tan(steer·δmax)/wheelbase·(drift ? 1.3 : 1)\n515\t       f = rotate(f, about u, yawRate·dt); r = u × f\n516\t     grip: vlat = v·r; maxDv = grip·surface.grip·(drift ? driftGrip : 1)·dt\n517\t           dv = clamp(−vlat, −maxDv, maxDv); v += r·dv; slide = |vlat| − |dv|\n518\t     v += a·dt;  p += v·dt;  p += n·(ride − d̄)·min(1, 25·dt)        (ride-height spring on position)\n519\t     car.n = n;  surface = most common surface_i;  boost pad: entering a boost collider while grounded ->\n520\t       v += f·CFG.boostDv (cap at 1.3·vtop), boostT = CFG.boostTime (re-arm after leaving that pad)\n521\t  5 AIRBORNE:\n522\t     v += g·dt;  v −= v·cdAir·|v|·dt;  p += v·dt;  air += dt\n523\t     f = rotate(f, about u, ctl.steer·airYaw·dt)                  (air steering)\n524\t     f = normalize(f + (v̂ − f)·min(1, 1.5·dt)); r = normalize(u × f); u = normalize(f × r)   (nose follows the arc)\n525\t     u = normalize(u + (ẑ − u)·min(1, 0.8·dt)), re-orthonormalize   (gentle roll levelling: no side landings after a\n526\t                                                                       mistimed loop)\n527\t  6 WALLS (both states, after moving): cast the chassis box (half extents L/2, W/2, 0.45 m; centre p + u·0.35 m;\n528\t     rotation from (f, r, u)) from the old to the new position with castShape (targetDistance 0.02 m). Ignore hits\n529\t     whose normal nw has |nw·u| > 0.65 (that's ground, step 3 owns it). On a wall hit: move to the contact\n530\t     (time_of_impact), vN = v·nw; v −= nw·vN·(1 + e) (e = 0.15); v *= 1 − 0.1·min(1, |vN|/10);\n531\t     turn f toward the wall tangent by up to 0.25 rad; slide the remaining motion once more; sparks at witness1;\n532\t     scrape sound while touching; |vN| > 15 m/s = crash (shake, rumble, big sparks). If the box starts overlapping\n533\t     a wall (intersectionsWithShape), restore the previous p and remove the inward velocity.\n534\t  7 LANE ASSIST (only on blocks with assist: loops): find the nearest centreline sample of the current block, lateral\n535\t     error e (along r) and its rate; f = rotate(f, about u, clamp(−0.35·e/1m − 0.08·ė/(1 m/s), −1, 1)·1.2·dt).\n536\t     CFG.loopAssist (on by default; a Setting and a Dev slider) scales it.\n537\t  8 FLOP: when landing on the side/roof (u·n < 0.3) or stuck upside down: 0.6 s animation that rotates the car\n538\t     upright onto the surface below, v *= 0.3, inputs ignored. Cartoonish, keeps flow; respawn is still one button.\n539\t  9 OUT OF BOUNDS: p.z < −25 m (fell into a chasm or off the world) -> auto-respawn after a 0.4 s fade.\n540\t```\n541\t\n542\tPrototype result (headless, Rapier 0.19.3 trimesh ribbons, G = 1.6 g, adhesion 0.35 g, ride 0.55 m, reach 0.9 m):\n543\tentering a 12 m-radius loop at 110 km/h, the car stayed grounded the whole way (≈ 80 km/h at the top, up = −0.99) and\n544\tleft it upright; a 20° kicker at ~110 km/h gave 2.4 s of air and an upright landing 50 m later. With averaged triangle\n545\tnormals instead of the four-point plane, the car detached on every flat facet — keep the plane fit. Without lane\n546\tassist, a loop whose exit is shifted sideways throws the car off its side — keep the assist on loop blocks.\n547\t\n548\t**Car tuning (defaults; all live in Dev Mode):**\n549\t\n550\t| | Coyote (Dustbowl) | Pebble (Hedgerow) | Moose (Frostpeak) |\n551\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n552\t| Body L×W×H (m) | 4.4 × 1.9 × 1.25 | 3.8 × 1.75 × 1.35 | 4.1 × 1.95 × 1.7 |\n553\t| Wheelbase / track / wheel radius (m) | 2.7 / 1.6 / 0.36 | 2.4 / 1.5 / 0.32 | 2.5 / 1.65 / 0.45 |\n554\t| ride (m) | 0.55 | 0.50 | 0.70 |\n555\t| vtop | 230 km/h | 195 km/h | 175 km/h |\n556\t| A0 (accel at 0) / B (brake) / Arev, vrev | 12 / 24 m/s² / 6, 40 km/h | 14 / 28 / 6, 40 | 11 / 22 / 6, 40 |\n557\t| δlo / δhi (steer at 0 / top speed) | 34° / 7° | 36° / 9° | 32° / 9° |\n558\t| grip (lateral, asphalt) | 15 m/s² | 18 m/s² | 14 m/s² |\n559\t| driftGrip | 0.55 | 0.70 | 0.60 |\n560\t| airYaw | 1.2 rad/s | 1.5 rad/s | 1.0 rad/s |\n561\t| cd / cdAir | 0.0004 /m | 0.0004 | 0.0005 |\n562\t| adhesion | 0.35 g | 0.35 g | 0.40 g |\n563\tGlobal: gravity 1.5 g; boostDv 10 m/s; boostAccel 7 m/s²; boostTime 1.2 s; wall e 0.15.\n564\t\n565\t**Surfaces** (`grip` multiplier per car, `roll` = rolling resistance m/s²):\n566\t\n567\t| Surface | Coyote | Pebble | Moose | roll | FX / sound |\n568\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n569\t| road (asphalt / tarmac / packed snow road) | 1.0 | 1.0 | 1.0 | 0.15 | tyre squeal |\n570\t| dirt | 0.75 | 0.95 | 0.85 | 0.6 | brown dust, crunch |\n571\t| grass (verge, embankment) | 0.55 | 0.60 | 0.65 | 2.5 | green bits |\n572\t| sand (Dustbowl plate) | 0.50 | 0.55 | 0.60 | 4.0 | sand plume |\n573\t| snow (Frostpeak plate, snowbank) | 0.60 | 0.65 | 0.90 | 1.2 | snow spray |\n574\t| ice | 0.30 | 0.35 | 0.55 | 0.05 | ice hiss, sparkles |\n575\t| boost | as road | | | 0.15 | chevrons flash |\n576\t\n577\t### 4.5 Cameras (`car/camera.js`; all through `world.camera` in `'fixed'` mode with `up`, E2)\n578\t\n579\tSet `world.camera.mouseLook = false` (no pointer lock in races). Compute in steps, place in `onDraw` interpolated with\n580\t`game.alpha` (the engine leaves a pose set in `onDraw` to the game).\n581\t- **Far chase (default):** target `T = p + u·1.2 m + f·3 m`; smoothed frame `fc` (forward) and `uc` (up) chase the\n582\t  car's `f, u` at 6/s and 4/s while grounded; in the air `fc` follows `v̂` and `uc` eases to ẑ at 1.5/s (the camera\n583\t  doesn't spin with flips). Position `T − fc·(6.5 m + 0.012 s·|v|) + uc·2.0 m`. FOV 70° + 12°·clamp((kmh − 100)/150,\n584\t  0, 1) + 6° while boosting (reduce-motion: no FOV kick). If a ray from T to the camera hits the track, pull in.\n585\t- **Close chase:** 4.2 m back, 1.3 m up, FOV 75°. **Hood:** `p + f·0.6 + u·1.15`, look along f, up u, FOV 80°; the\n586\t  pen draws the bonnet and a dashboard strip (the overlay pen, as the shooter kit draws a gun) so it reads as a car.\n587\t- **Flyover (intro):** samples the route; the camera rides 25 m above and 30 m beside the route from start to finish\n588\t  over 2.5 s (smoothstep), then cuts behind the car.\n589\t- **Finish orbit:** 10 m radius around the car, 0.35 rad/s, slight slow-motion (`game.timeScale = .35` for 0.6 s).\n590\t- **TV (replays):** trackside spots generated along the route every ~5 blocks, 25 m to the side and 6 m up; the\n591\t  nearest spot with a clear line of sight films; FOV narrows to keep the car ~1/4 of screen height.\n592\t- **Orbit/free (replays, results):** right stick / mouse drag orbit, triggers / wheel zoom.\n593\t- **Editor:** orbit around the cursor (yaw, pitch 25°–80°, distance 60–400 m), smoothed (§5.4).\n594\t- Split screen: one `world.addCamera()` per extra viewport, each with its own chase state.\n595\t\n596\t### 4.6 A run (`race/run.js`)\n597\t\n598\t- Phases: `intro` (flyover) → `countdown` (3 s; 1 s on restart) → `racing` → `finished` | `abandoned`.\n599\t- The clock counts **steps** from GO; the car is held (brakes on, gas revs the engine sound only) before GO.\n600\t- **Gates:** each CP/finish gate is a plane (point, normal = path tangent, half-width = road half-width + 1 m,\n601\t  height 7 m above the road along u). A crossing = the segment from the previous to the new car position crosses\n602\t  the plane within those bounds. **Checkpoints count once each, in any order, either direction** (TrackMania).\n603\t  **Finish counts only forward and only with every checkpoint passed**; otherwise show \"MISSING CHECKPOINT\" once.\n604\t- **Respawn:** to the last checkpoint passed (or the start): car at the gate (or spawn) frame, `v = 0`, upright,\n605\t  `boostT = 0`; the clock keeps running; respawn counter +1; warp-in FX (glints, a quick scale-in, rising arpeggio).\n606\t- **Restart:** new run object; ghost recording restarts; respawn counter 0.\n607\t- **Splits:** per run, the step count at each CP in the order passed; compare to the best run's splits (by order).\n608\t- Events emitted for HUD/sound/FX: `cp(i, steps, delta)`, `finish(steps, delta, medal)`, `respawn`, `restart`,\n609\t  `boost`, `land(impact)`, `wall(impact)`, `flop`, `missingCp`.\n610\t\n611\t### 4.7 Ghosts and replays (`race/ghost.js`)\n612\t\n613\t- Record every 4th step (30 Hz): position (int16 deltas in 1/16 unit — 1/256 m; a key frame every 30 samples with\n614\t  float32 absolutes), orientation (smallest-three quaternion, int16), speed (uint8 km/h/2), flags (grounded, boost,\n615\t  brake). ≈ 15 KB per minute; stored base64 in the profile (best run per track, 10 replay slots).\n616\t- Playback: interpolate position (lerp) and orientation (slerp) at any time; wheel spin and steering are derived\n617\t  (speed, yaw rate). Ghost cars draw with `pen.ghost = true` (E3) in a light tint of their paint.\n618\t- A **replay** is a ghost plus metadata (track id or embedded custom track, car, paint, time, date, events with step\n619\t  numbers: CPs, respawns, finish).\n620\t- Coco's ghost (author run) is not stored: regenerate it by running the bot (deterministic, ~0.2 s) when needed.\n621\t\n622\t### 4.8 The autopilot (`race/bot.js`) — used by tests, medal baking, Survival rivals, attract mode, Dev Mode\n623\t\n624\t1. **Route:** walk links from Start's exit port to Finish, following each block's path in the traversed direction\n625\t   and jump links over gaps; crossings go straight through. Sample every 2 m: `{ p, t, u, r, halfWidth (road/2 −\n626\t   1.2 m), surface, flags: kicker|landing|loop|boost|gate, block }`. A route that doesn't reach Finish is an editor\n627\t   error (\"Route broken at ...\").\n628\t2. **Racing line:** lateral offsets e_i ∈ [−hw, +hw], start at 0, 80 iterations of curvature smoothing with clamping\n629\t   (`e_i ← clamp(e_i + 0.5·((e_{i−1} + e_{i+1})/2 − e_i) − 0.3·κ_i·hw, −hw, hw)`, κ signed in the surface plane); force\n630\t   e = 0 on loops, kickers, landings, gates and boost pads (the line goes through pads).\n631\t3. **Speed profile:** `vmax_i = min(vtop·1.3, sqrt(a_lat / |κ_i|))`, a_lat = skillGrip·grip·surfaceGrip (+ g·sin(bank)\n632\t   on banks); full speed through loops and kickers; then a backward pass with braking B·skillBrake and a forward pass\n633\t   with the car's acceleration curve. Flag tracks where the speed before a kicker is below what its gap needs\n634\t   (`v ≥ sqrt(g·gapLength/sin(30°))`·1.1) — a test fails on that.\n635\t4. **Control (each step):** nearest route index (search a ±15-sample window after the last one, by 3D distance — never\n636\t   jump between a loop's two lanes); lookahead point at `6 m + 0.35 s·|v|`; α = angle to it in the car's (f, r)\n637\t   plane; `steer = clamp(1.6·α/δmax(v))`; `gas = 1` if v < target − 0.5 m/s; `brake = clamp((v − target)/5)` if\n638\t   v > target + 1 m/s; in the air: steer 0, gas 1.\n639\t5. **Recovery:** off the route by more than hw + 3 m for 0.6 s, slower than 1 m/s for 1.5 s after GO, or two flops in\n640\t   a row → respawn.\n641\t6. **Skill 0..1:** grip use 0.75 + 0.25·skill, brake margin ×(1.25 − 0.25·skill), lookahead jitter ±0.4 m·(1 −\n642\t   skill) from `E.rng(seed)`, a lazy line (e scaled by 0.6 + 0.4·skill). Skill 1, no cheats = the **author** driver.\n643\t7. **Cheats (attract/demo only):** lane snap (pull p toward the line, 4 m/s max), +10% grip, auto-respawn instantly.\n644\t\n645\t### 4.9 Medals (`race/medals.js`, `tools/bake.mjs`)\n646\t\n647\t- Author time = the bot at skill 1 without cheats (campaign and puzzle reference solutions), baked by\n648\t  `node tools/bake.mjs` into `src/data/medals.json` (`{ id: { author, gold, silver, bronze } }` in steps). Re-bake\n649\t  after any tuning change (Dev Mode has \"Re-bake this track\" for live tuning; tests fail if a baked value no longer\n650\t  matches a fresh bot run within 1 step).\n651\t- **Gold = author × 1.06 rounded up to 0.1 s; Silver = × 1.2 rounded up to 1 s; Bronze = × 1.5 rounded up to 1 s**\n652\t  (TrackMania's ratios). Multipliers are Dev sliders; a track may carry `medalScale` to adjust.\n653\t- Editor tracks: author = your validation time; the same ratios.\n654\t- Medal icons carry letters (B, S, G, A). The Author medal is \"Coco's Time\".\n655\t\n656\t---\n657\t\n658\t## 5. Modes and features\n659\t\n660\t### 5.1 Profile, progression and the coppers economy (`save/profile.js`, `modes/campaign.js`)\n661\t\n662\tProfile (one per browser; `E.store` key `crackmania:profile`, `version: 1`, with a `migrate()` hook): name (letter\n663\twheel), coppers, per-track records `{ bestSteps, bestSplits, medal: 0..4, ghost, attempts }`, puzzle records, survival\n664\tbest rank per gauntlet, unlocked packs and patterns, garage paint per car, 6 custom track slots, 10 replay slots, seen\n665\tstory beats, first-time tips seen. In AI Hub sessions the hub gives the page empty, temporary storage: nothing to do.\n666\t\n667\t**Coppers (¢).** Start with **300 ¢**. Rewards are paid **once per medal tier** (earning Gold first time pays Bronze +\n668\tSilver + Gold):\n669\t\n670\t| | Bronze | Silver | Gold | Author |\n671\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n672\t| Race (× env: Dustbowl 1, Hedgerow 1.25, Frostpeak 1.5) | 60 | 90 | 150 | 300 |\n673\t| Puzzle | 80 | 120 | 200 | 300 |\n674\tSurvival: 50 ¢ per round survived beyond your previous best for that gauntlet, plus 300 ¢ the first time a gauntlet is\n675\tcleared. Dev slider: copper multiplier.\n676\t\n677\t**Spending.** Editor blocks cost coppers when placed (refunded 100% when removed; table §4.1). Editor **packs** unlock\n678\tfamilies of blocks: BASIC (start, finish, checkpoint, straights, turns, hills, crossing) free; STUNTS (kicker, landing,\n679\tboost, bumps) 250 ¢; LOOPS & BANKS 600 ¢; SURFACES (dirt, ice, snow variants) 200 ¢; SCENERY 150 ¢. Garage patterns:\n680\t3 free, the other 5 at 100 ¢ each. Prices show on every tile; \"Not enough coppers\" plays the error buzz and shakes the\n681\twallet.\n682\t\n683\t**Unlocks.**\n684\t- Dustbowl D1 and D2 open at start; each next track opens when the previous one has any medal.\n685\t- An environment's **Puzzles** open when its 2nd race has a medal; its **Survival** when its 3rd race has a medal.\n686\t- **Hedgerow** opens with medals on 3 Dustbowl races; **Frostpeak** with medals on 3 Hedgerow races.\n687\t- Build, Hot Seat, Split Screen, Garage and Replays are open from the start (MP modes offer every track of unlocked\n688\t  environments plus custom tracks).\n689\t- Story beats fire on these events (§8.2). Golds on all 15 race tracks trigger the ending and the credits roll.\n690\t\n691\t### 5.2 Race (campaign)\n692\t\n693\tFront end: **Environment select** (three big cards with the car, the env emblem, medal count `G 3/5`, a lock with the\n694\trequirement) → **Track select** (5 tiles: number, name, a baked minimap of the route, best time, medal icon, lock;\n695\t△ toggles \"race Coco's ghost\") → run (§4.6) → **Results** (time big; best and delta; medal drop-in with sting; next\n696\tmedal target \"SILVER 0:31\"; coppers count-up; buttons **Retry** (△ / R), **Next track** (✕ / Enter), **Replay** (□ /\n697\tV), **Save replay**, **Menu** (○ / Esc)). Pause menu items in races: Resume, Restart, Respawn, Camera, Ghosts,\n698\t**Dev Mode**, Settings, Controls, Quit to menu (`menu.items` may be a function; check the engine's `v(...)` wrapper\n699\tand return per-scene items).\n700\t\n701\tHUD (`ui/hud.js`, per viewport): top centre timer `0:23.41` (big digits); under it, for 2 s after a CP, the split and\n702\tdelta; top left `CP 1/3` with a flag icon and the respawn count if > 0; top right the next medal target with its icon\n703\t(and \"BEST 0:31.20\" under it); bottom right speed (big digits + `KM/H`, or MPH by setting) and a boost flame icon while\n704\tboosting; centre: countdown digits (3 → 2 → 1 → GO!, scale 6, pop tween), \"MISSING CHECKPOINT\", \"FINISH!\", \"NEW\n705\tRECORD!\". Bottom centre after a flop or when stopped for 2 s: prompt `○ Respawn  △ Restart`. Edge vignette + speed\n706\tlines above 200 km/h (reduce-motion: off).\n707\t\n708\t### 5.3 Puzzle (`modes/puzzle.js`; runs inside the editor scene)\n709\t\n710\tA puzzle = environment, **fixed blocks** (start, checkpoints, finish; sometimes more), a **build zone** (rectangle of\n711\tcells and levels), **no-build cells** (chasms, hedges, rocks, a pond — drawn as such), an **inventory** (block type →\n712\tcount) and a reference solution (for its author time and for tests). The editor runs in puzzle mode: the palette shows\n713\tonly inventory blocks with remaining counts (`R2 ×1`), fixed blocks show a lock and can't be moved, placement outside\n714\tthe zone is refused, no coppers are spent. **Validate** = drive from start through all CPs to finish; medals by time\n715\tagainst the solution's baked thresholds. Several routes are possible; the inventory includes extra pieces so a smarter\n716\troute (a boost, a wider bend) beats the obvious one. First-time Coco tip explains it in three lines.\n717\t\n718\t### 5.4 Build — the track editor (`editor/editor.js`)\n719\t\n720\tOpening: environment and slot select (6 slots with names, env emblem, validated mark and author time) → the editor.\n721\t\n722\tScreen: the 3D track with an **orbit camera** around the cursor; a translucent **grid** at the cursor's level (pen\n723\tbars every cell within 6 cells of the cursor, brighter on the cursor's row/column); the **cursor** (a pulsing cell\n724\toutline + a ghost preview of the selected block, green if it fits, red if it collides / is outside the grid / you\n725\tcan't afford it; small arrows on its ports, blue when they'd link); placed blocks' open ports show red arrows. Top\n726\tbar: track name, env, coppers (or puzzle counts), status chips `START ✓ FINISH ✓ CP 2 ROUTE ✓ VALIDATED 0:41.20`.\n727\tBottom: the **palette** carousel (categories ROADS / TURNS / HILLS / STUNTS / SURFACES / SCENERY as tabs; 48×36 px\n728\ticons baked top-down from each block's geometry; name, cost, lock if the pack isn't owned). Left: a short prompt list.\n729\t\n730\t| Action | DualSense | Keyboard / mouse |\n731\t| --- | --- | --- |\n732\t| move cursor (camera-relative, repeats) | left stick | WASD / arrows; mouse hover picks the cell under the pointer on the cursor's level (ray–plane) |\n733\t| palette item / category | d-pad ←/→ / ↑/↓ | Tab / Shift+Tab categories, 1–9 items, mouse click on a tile |\n734\t| place | ✕ | Space / Enter / left click |\n735\t| remove block under cursor | □ | Delete / Backspace / right click |\n736\t| rotate selected block | R1 (cw) / L1 (ccw) | R / Shift+R / mouse wheel |\n737\t| level up / down | R2 / L2 | E / Q / Shift+wheel / PageUp / PageDown |\n738\t| orbit / tilt camera | right stick | middle-drag or Alt+left-drag; wheel+Ctrl zooms |\n739\t| test drive from Start | △ | T |\n740\t| undo / redo | L3 / R3 | Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y |\n741\t| editor menu | Options | Esc |\n742\t\n743\tEditor menu: Resume, **Validate** (a run from Start; finishing with every CP sets the author time and medals; any\n744\tedit afterwards clears it), Test drive, Save, Save as, Load, Rename (letter wheel), Environment (only when empty),\n745\tShare code (shows a base64url code in a large box; Copy uses `navigator.clipboard` when allowed), Import code (a text\n746\tfield; keyboard paste), Clear track (asks), Dev Mode, Settings, Exit. Test drive returns to the same cursor and\n747\tcamera. Undo/redo stack of 200 operations (place, remove, rotate, rename) with coppers refunded/charged.\n748\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"39f9fe98-25b4-4b7d-bcba-64520a01a5a6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:39:24.181Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work/PLAN.md","content":"     coast: if gas = 0: a −= v̂·1.2 m/s²;  rolling: a −= v̂·surface.roll;  aero: a −= v·cd·|v|\n     boost: if boostT > 0: a += f·CFG.boostAccel; boostT −= dt\n     steering (bicycle model): δmax = lerp(δlo, δhi, clamp(|s|/vtop, 0, 1)^0.7)\n       steerIn: keyboard input ramps to ±1 over 0.12 s and back over 0.08 s; sticks apply directly (deadzone by engine)\n       drift = brake > 0.5 && |steer| > 0.5 && s > 60 km/h (TrackMania's brake-drift)\n       yawRate = s·tan(steer·δmax)/wheelbase·(drift ? 1.3 : 1)\n       f = rotate(f, about u, yawRate·dt); r = u × f\n     grip: vlat = v·r; maxDv = grip·surface.grip·(drift ? driftGrip : 1)·dt\n           dv = clamp(−vlat, −maxDv, maxDv); v += r·dv; slide = |vlat| − |dv|\n     v += a·dt;  p += v·dt;  p += n·(ride − d̄)·min(1, 25·dt)        (ride-height spring on position)\n     car.n = n;  surface = most common surface_i;  boost pad: entering a boost collider while grounded ->\n       v += f·CFG.boostDv (cap at 1.3·vtop), boostT = CFG.boostTime (re-arm after leaving that pad)\n  5 AIRBORNE:\n     v += g·dt;  v −= v·cdAir·|v|·dt;  p += v·dt;  air += dt\n     f = rotate(f, about u, ctl.steer·airYaw·dt)                  (air steering)\n     f = normalize(f + (v̂ − f)·min(1, 1.5·dt)); r = normalize(u × f); u = normalize(f × r)   (nose follows the arc)\n     u = normalize(u + (ẑ − u)·min(1, 0.8·dt)), re-orthonormalize   (gentle roll levelling: no side landings after a\n                                                                       mistimed loop)\n  6 WALLS (both states, after moving): cast the chassis box (half extents L/2, W/2, 0.45 m; centre p + u·0.35 m;\n     rotation from (f, r, u)) from the old to the new position with castShape (targetDistance 0.02 m). Ignore hits\n     whose normal nw has |nw·u| > 0.65 (that's ground, step 3 owns it). On a wall hit: move to the contact\n     (time_of_impact), vN = v·nw; v −= nw·vN·(1 + e) (e = 0.15); v *= 1 − 0.1·min(1, |vN|/10);\n     turn f toward the wall tangent by up to 0.25 rad; slide the remaining motion once more; sparks at witness1;\n     scrape sound while touching; |vN| > 15 m/s = crash (shake, rumble, big sparks). If the box starts overlapping\n     a wall (intersectionsWithShape), restore the previous p and remove the inward velocity.\n  7 LANE ASSIST (only on blocks with assist: loops): find the nearest centreline sample of the current block, lateral\n     error e (along r) and its rate; f = rotate(f, about u, clamp(−0.35·e/1m − 0.08·ė/(1 m/s), −1, 1)·1.2·dt).\n     CFG.loopAssist (on by default; a Setting and a Dev slider) scales it.\n  8 FLOP: when landing on the side/roof (u·n < 0.3) or stuck upside down: 0.6 s animation that rotates the car\n     upright onto the surface below, v *= 0.3, inputs ignored. Cartoonish, keeps flow; respawn is still one button.\n  9 OUT OF BOUNDS: p.z < −25 m (fell into a chasm or off the world) -> auto-respawn after a 0.4 s fade.\n```\n\nPrototype result (headless, Rapier 0.19.3 trimesh ribbons, G = 1.6 g, adhesion 0.35 g, ride 0.55 m, reach 0.9 m):\nentering a 12 m-radius loop at 110 km/h, the car stayed grounded the whole way (≈ 80 km/h at the top, up = −0.99) and\nleft it upright; a 20° kicker at ~110 km/h gave 2.4 s of air and an upright landing 50 m later. With averaged triangle\nnormals instead of the four-point plane, the car detached on every flat facet — keep the plane fit. Without lane\nassist, a loop whose exit is shifted sideways throws the car off its side — keep the assist on loop blocks.\n\n**Car tuning (defaults; all live in Dev Mode):**\n\n| | Coyote (Dustbowl) | Pebble (Hedgerow) | Moose (Frostpeak) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Body L×W×H (m) | 4.4 × 1.9 × 1.25 | 3.8 × 1.75 × 1.35 | 4.1 × 1.95 × 1.7 |\n| Wheelbase / track / wheel radius (m) | 2.7 / 1.6 / 0.36 | 2.4 / 1.5 / 0.32 | 2.5 / 1.65 / 0.45 |\n| ride (m) | 0.55 | 0.50 | 0.70 |\n| vtop | 230 km/h | 195 km/h | 175 km/h |\n| A0 (accel at 0) / B (brake) / Arev, vrev | 12 / 24 m/s² / 6, 40 km/h | 14 / 28 / 6, 40 | 11 / 22 / 6, 40 |\n| δlo / δhi (steer at 0 / top speed) | 34° / 7° | 36° / 9° | 32° / 9° |\n| grip (lateral, asphalt) | 15 m/s² | 18 m/s² | 14 m/s² |\n| driftGrip | 0.55 | 0.70 | 0.60 |\n| airYaw | 1.2 rad/s | 1.5 rad/s | 1.0 rad/s |\n| cd / cdAir | 0.0004 /m | 0.0004 | 0.0005 |\n| adhesion | 0.35 g | 0.35 g | 0.40 g |\nGlobal: gravity 1.5 g; boostDv 10 m/s; boostAccel 7 m/s²; boostTime 1.2 s; wall e 0.15.\n\n**Surfaces** (`grip` multiplier per car, `roll` = rolling resistance m/s²):\n\n| Surface | Coyote | Pebble | Moose | roll | FX / sound |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| road (asphalt / tarmac / packed snow road) | 1.0 | 1.0 | 1.0 | 0.15 | tyre squeal |\n| dirt | 0.75 | 0.95 | 0.85 | 0.6 | brown dust, crunch |\n| grass (verge, embankment) | 0.55 | 0.60 | 0.65 | 2.5 | green bits |\n| sand (Dustbowl plate) | 0.50 | 0.55 | 0.60 | 4.0 | sand plume |\n| snow (Frostpeak plate, snowbank) | 0.60 | 0.65 | 0.90 | 1.2 | snow spray |\n| ice | 0.30 | 0.35 | 0.55 | 0.05 | ice hiss, sparkles |\n| boost | as road | | | 0.15 | chevrons flash |\n\n### 4.5 Cameras (`car/camera.js`; all through `world.camera` in `'fixed'` mode with `up`, E2)\n\nSet `world.camera.mouseLook = false` (no pointer lock in races). Compute in steps, place in `onDraw` interpolated with\n`game.alpha` (the engine leaves a pose set in `onDraw` to the game).\n- **Far chase (default):** target `T = p + u·1.2 m + f·3 m`; smoothed frame `fc` (forward) and `uc` (up) chase the\n  car's `f, u` at 6/s and 4/s while grounded; in the air `fc` follows `v̂` and `uc` eases to ẑ at 1.5/s (the camera\n  doesn't spin with flips). Position `T − fc·(6.5 m + 0.012 s·|v|) + uc·2.0 m`. FOV 70° + 12°·clamp((kmh − 100)/150,\n  0, 1) + 6° while boosting (reduce-motion: no FOV kick). If a ray from T to the camera hits the track, pull in.\n- **Close chase:** 4.2 m back, 1.3 m up, FOV 75°. **Hood:** `p + f·0.6 + u·1.15`, look along f, up u, FOV 80°; the\n  pen draws the bonnet and a dashboard strip (the overlay pen, as the shooter kit draws a gun) so it reads as a car.\n- **Flyover (intro):** samples the route; the camera rides 25 m above and 30 m beside the route from start to finish\n  over 2.5 s (smoothstep), then cuts behind the car.\n- **Finish orbit:** 10 m radius around the car, 0.35 rad/s, slight slow-motion (`game.timeScale = .35` for 0.6 s).\n- **TV (replays):** trackside spots generated along the route every ~5 blocks, 25 m to the side and 6 m up; the\n  nearest spot with a clear line of sight films; FOV narrows to keep the car ~1/4 of screen height.\n- **Orbit/free (replays, results):** right stick / mouse drag orbit, triggers / wheel zoom.\n- **Editor:** orbit around the cursor (yaw, pitch 25°–80°, distance 60–400 m), smoothed (§5.4).\n- Split screen: one `world.addCamera()` per extra viewport, each with its own chase state.\n\n### 4.6 A run (`race/run.js`)\n\n- Phases: `intro` (flyover) → `countdown` (3 s; 1 s on restart) → `racing` → `finished` | `abandoned`.\n- The clock counts **steps** from GO; the car is held (brakes on, gas revs the engine sound only) before GO.\n- **Gates:** each CP/finish gate is a plane (point, normal = path tangent, half-width = road half-width + 1 m,\n  height 7 m above the road along u). A crossing = the segment from the previous to the new car position crosses\n  the plane within those bounds. **Checkpoints count once each, in any order, either direction** (TrackMania).\n  **Finish counts only forward and only with every checkpoint passed**; otherwise show \"MISSING CHECKPOINT\" once.\n- **Respawn:** to the last checkpoint passed (or the start): car at the gate (or spawn) frame, `v = 0`, upright,\n  `boostT = 0`; the clock keeps running; respawn counter +1; warp-in FX (glints, a quick scale-in, rising arpeggio).\n- **Restart:** new run object; ghost recording restarts; respawn counter 0.\n- **Splits:** per run, the step count at each CP in the order passed; compare to the best run's splits (by order).\n- Events emitted for HUD/sound/FX: `cp(i, steps, delta)`, `finish(steps, delta, medal)`, `respawn`, `restart`,\n  `boost`, `land(impact)`, `wall(impact)`, `flop`, `missingCp`.\n\n### 4.7 Ghosts and replays (`race/ghost.js`)\n\n- Record every 4th step (30 Hz): position (int16 deltas in 1/16 unit — 1/256 m; a key frame every 30 samples with\n  float32 absolutes), orientation (smallest-three quaternion, int16), speed (uint8 km/h/2), flags (grounded, boost,\n  brake). ≈ 15 KB per minute; stored base64 in the profile (best run per track, 10 replay slots).\n- Playback: interpolate position (lerp) and orientation (slerp) at any time; wheel spin and steering are derived\n  (speed, yaw rate). Ghost cars draw with `pen.ghost = true` (E3) in a light tint of their paint.\n- A **replay** is a ghost plus metadata (track id or embedded custom track, car, paint, time, date, events with step\n  numbers: CPs, respawns, finish).\n- Coco's ghost (author run) is not stored: regenerate it by running the bot (deterministic, ~0.2 s) when needed.\n\n### 4.8 The autopilot (`race/bot.js`) — used by tests, medal baking, Survival rivals, attract mode, Dev Mode\n\n1. **Route:** walk links from Start's exit port to Finish, following each block's path in the traversed direction\n   and jump links over gaps; crossings go straight through. Sample every 2 m: `{ p, t, u, r, halfWidth (road/2 −\n   1.2 m), surface, flags: kicker|landing|loop|boost|gate, block }`. A route that doesn't reach Finish is an editor\n   error (\"Route broken at ...\").\n2. **Racing line:** lateral offsets e_i ∈ [−hw, +hw], start at 0, 80 iterations of curvature smoothing with clamping\n   (`e_i ← clamp(e_i + 0.5·((e_{i−1} + e_{i+1})/2 − e_i) − 0.3·κ_i·hw, −hw, hw)`, κ signed in the surface plane); force\n   e = 0 on loops, kickers, landings, gates and boost pads (the line goes through pads).\n3. **Speed profile:** `vmax_i = min(vtop·1.3, sqrt(a_lat / |κ_i|))`, a_lat = skillGrip·grip·surfaceGrip (+ g·sin(bank)\n   on banks); full speed through loops and kickers; then a backward pass with braking B·skillBrake and a forward pass\n   with the car's acceleration curve. Flag tracks where the speed before a kicker is below what its gap needs\n   (`v ≥ sqrt(g·gapLength/sin(30°))`·1.1) — a test fails on that.\n4. **Control (each step):** nearest route index (search a ±15-sample window after the last one, by 3D distance — never\n   jump between a loop's two lanes); lookahead point at `6 m + 0.35 s·|v|`; α = angle to it in the car's (f, r)\n   plane; `steer = clamp(1.6·α/δmax(v))`; `gas = 1` if v < target − 0.5 m/s; `brake = clamp((v − target)/5)` if\n   v > target + 1 m/s; in the air: steer 0, gas 1.\n5. **Recovery:** off the route by more than hw + 3 m for 0.6 s, slower than 1 m/s for 1.5 s after GO, or two flops in\n   a row → respawn.\n6. **Skill 0..1:** grip use 0.75 + 0.25·skill, brake margin ×(1.25 − 0.25·skill), lookahead jitter ±0.4 m·(1 −\n   skill) from `E.rng(seed)`, a lazy line (e scaled by 0.6 + 0.4·skill). Skill 1, no cheats = the **author** driver.\n7. **Cheats (attract/demo only):** lane snap (pull p toward the line, 4 m/s max), +10% grip, auto-respawn instantly.\n\n### 4.9 Medals (`race/medals.js`, `tools/bake.mjs`)\n\n- Author time = the bot at skill 1 without cheats (campaign and puzzle reference solutions), baked by\n  `node tools/bake.mjs` into `src/data/medals.json` (`{ id: { author, gold, silver, bronze } }` in steps). Re-bake\n  after any tuning change (Dev Mode has \"Re-bake this track\" for live tuning; tests fail if a baked value no longer\n  matches a fresh bot run within 1 step).\n- **Gold = author × 1.06 rounded up to 0.1 s; Silver = × 1.2 rounded up to 1 s; Bronze = × 1.5 rounded up to 1 s**\n  (TrackMania's ratios). Multipliers are Dev sliders; a track may carry `medalScale` to adjust.\n- Editor tracks: author = your validation time; the same ratios.\n- Medal icons carry letters (B, S, G, A). The Author medal is \"Coco's Time\".\n\n---\n\n## 5. Modes and features\n\n### 5.1 Profile, progression and the coppers economy (`save/profile.js`, `modes/campaign.js`)\n\nProfile (one per browser; `E.store` key `crackmania:profile`, `version: 1`, with a `migrate()` hook): name (letter\nwheel), coppers, per-track records `{ bestSteps, bestSplits, medal: 0..4, ghost, attempts }`, puzzle records, survival\nbest rank per gauntlet, unlocked packs and patterns, garage paint per car, 6 custom track slots, 10 replay slots, seen\nstory beats, first-time tips seen. In AI Hub sessions the hub gives the page empty, temporary storage: nothing to do.\n\n**Coppers (¢).** Start with **300 ¢**. Rewards are paid **once per medal tier** (earning Gold first time pays Bronze +\nSilver + Gold):\n\n| | Bronze | Silver | Gold | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Race (× env: Dustbowl 1, Hedgerow 1.25, Frostpeak 1.5) | 60 | 90 | 150 | 300 |\n| Puzzle | 80 | 120 | 200 | 300 |\nSurvival: 50 ¢ per round survived beyond your previous best for that gauntlet, plus 300 ¢ the first time a gauntlet is\ncleared. Dev slider: copper multiplier.\n\n**Spending.** Editor blocks cost coppers when placed (refunded 100% when removed; table §4.1). Editor **packs** unlock\nfamilies of blocks: BASIC (start, finish, checkpoint, straights, turns, hills, crossing) free; STUNTS (kicker, landing,\nboost, bumps) 250 ¢; LOOPS & BANKS 600 ¢; SURFACES (dirt, ice, snow variants) 200 ¢; SCENERY 150 ¢. Garage patterns:\n3 free, the other 5 at 100 ¢ each. Prices show on every tile; \"Not enough coppers\" plays the error buzz and shakes the\nwallet.\n\n**Unlocks.**\n- Dustbowl D1 and D2 open at start; each next track opens when the previous one has any medal.\n- An environment's **Puzzles** open when its 2nd race has a medal; its **Survival** when its 3rd race has a medal.\n- **Hedgerow** opens with medals on 3 Dustbowl races; **Frostpeak** with medals on 3 Hedgerow races.\n- Build, Hot Seat, Split Screen, Garage and Replays are open from the start (MP modes offer every track of unlocked\n  environments plus custom tracks).\n- Story beats fire on these events (§8.2). Golds on all 15 race tracks trigger the ending and the credits roll.\n\n### 5.2 Race (campaign)\n\nFront end: **Environment select** (three big cards with the car, the env emblem, medal count `G 3/5`, a lock with the\nrequirement) → **Track select** (5 tiles: number, name, a baked minimap of the route, best time, medal icon, lock;\n△ toggles \"race Coco's ghost\") → run (§4.6) → **Results** (time big; best and delta; medal drop-in with sting; next\nmedal target \"SILVER 0:31\"; coppers count-up; buttons **Retry** (△ / R), **Next track** (✕ / Enter), **Replay** (□ /\nV), **Save replay**, **Menu** (○ / Esc)). Pause menu items in races: Resume, Restart, Respawn, Camera, Ghosts,\n**Dev Mode**, Settings, Controls, Quit to menu (`menu.items` may be a function; check the engine's `v(...)` wrapper\nand return per-scene items).\n\nHUD (`ui/hud.js`, per viewport): top centre timer `0:23.41` (big digits); under it, for 2 s after a CP, the split and\ndelta; top left `CP 1/3` with a flag icon and the respawn count if > 0; top right the next medal target with its icon\n(and \"BEST 0:31.20\" under it); bottom right speed (big digits + `KM/H`, or MPH by setting) and a boost flame icon while\nboosting; centre: countdown digits (3 → 2 → 1 → GO!, scale 6, pop tween), \"MISSING CHECKPOINT\", \"FINISH!\", \"NEW\nRECORD!\". Bottom centre after a flop or when stopped for 2 s: prompt `○ Respawn  △ Restart`. Edge vignette + speed\nlines above 200 km/h (reduce-motion: off).\n\n### 5.3 Puzzle (`modes/puzzle.js`; runs inside the editor scene)\n\nA puzzle = environment, **fixed blocks** (start, checkpoints, finish; sometimes more), a **build zone** (rectangle of\ncells and levels), **no-build cells** (chasms, hedges, rocks, a pond — drawn as such), an **inventory** (block type →\ncount) and a reference solution (for its author time and for tests). The editor runs in puzzle mode: the palette shows\nonly inventory blocks with remaining counts (`R2 ×1`), fixed blocks show a lock and can't be moved, placement outside\nthe zone is refused, no coppers are spent. **Validate** = drive from start through all CPs to finish; medals by time\nagainst the solution's baked thresholds. Several routes are possible; the inventory includes extra pieces so a smarter\nroute (a boost, a wider bend) beats the obvious one. First-time Coco tip explains it in three lines.\n\n### 5.4 Build — the track editor (`editor/editor.js`)\n\nOpening: environment and slot select (6 slots with names, env emblem, validated mark and author time) → the editor.\n\nScreen: the 3D track with an **orbit camera** around the cursor; a translucent **grid** at the cursor's level (pen\nbars every cell within 6 cells of the cursor, brighter on the cursor's row/column); the **cursor** (a pulsing cell\noutline + a ghost preview of the selected block, green if it fits, red if it collides / is outside the grid / you\ncan't afford it; small arrows on its ports, blue when they'd link); placed blocks' open ports show red arrows. Top\nbar: track name, env, coppers (or puzzle counts), status chips `START ✓ FINISH ✓ CP 2 ROUTE ✓ VALIDATED 0:41.20`.\nBottom: the **palette** carousel (categories ROADS / TURNS / HILLS / STUNTS / SURFACES / SCENERY as tabs; 48×36 px\nicons baked top-down from each block's geometry; name, cost, lock if the pack isn't owned). Left: a short prompt list.\n\n| Action | DualSense | Keyboard / mouse |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| move cursor (camera-relative, repeats) | left stick | WASD / arrows; mouse hover picks the cell under the pointer on the cursor's level (ray–plane) |\n| palette item / category | d-pad ←/→ / ↑/↓ | Tab / Shift+Tab categories, 1–9 items, mouse click on a tile |\n| place | ✕ | Space / Enter / left click |\n| remove block under cursor | □ | Delete / Backspace / right click |\n| rotate selected block | R1 (cw) / L1 (ccw) | R / Shift+R / mouse wheel |\n| level up / down | R2 / L2 | E / Q / Shift+wheel / PageUp / PageDown |\n| orbit / tilt camera | right stick | middle-drag or Alt+left-drag; wheel+Ctrl zooms |\n| test drive from Start | △ | T |\n| undo / redo | L3 / R3 | Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y |\n| editor menu | Options | Esc |\n\nEditor menu: Resume, **Validate** (a run from Start; finishing with every CP sets the author time and medals; any\nedit afterwards clears it), Test drive, Save, Save as, Load, Rename (letter wheel), Environment (only when empty),\nShare code (shows a base64url code in a large box; Copy uses `navigator.clipboard` when allowed), Import code (a text\nfield; keyboard paste), Clear track (asks), Dev Mode, Settings, Exit. Test drive returns to the same cursor and\ncamera. Undo/redo stack of 200 operations (place, remove, rotate, rename) with coppers refunded/charged.\n","numLines":240,"startLine":509,"totalLines":1416}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CBkS32eHVqusKDaomcgJx2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
