{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2xuwZovRMjF22udZy5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9803,"cache_read_input_tokens":505098,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9803},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"d7dc5a23-8478-41a8-9554-ea6672ea85e2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:39:29.534Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2xugwPS4q5JbYEfRLv","thinking_duration_ms":4290,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2xuwZovRMjF22udZy5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GSf9C3AJAgegUizacAMkhD","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work/PLAN.md","offset":748,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9803,"cache_read_input_tokens":505098,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9803},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"97d8b44c-93fa-4ba8-abb4-c39b01a8b6e6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:39:31.062Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2xugwPS4q5JbYEfRLv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GSf9C3AJAgegUizacAMkhD":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work/PLAN.md","offset":748,"limit":200}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GSf9C3AJAgegUizacAMkhD","type":"tool_result","content":"748\t\n749\tRules: one Start (free), at least one Finish (free), any number of CPs; blocks can't overlap (3D occupancy) but can\n750\tsit above others with ≥ 1 level of clearance (supports are generated automatically and never block a lane under\n751\tthem); gaps under kickers are reserved automatically when a kicker is placed (shown hatched). A track is shareable\n752\tand playable in Hot Seat / Split Screen once validated. A Dev Mode button \"Export as content\" prints a `data/tracks.js`\n753\tentry (placements + metadata) — the designer workflow for growing the game later.\n754\t\n755\t### 5.5 Survival (`modes/survival.js`)\n756\t\n757\tPer environment a **gauntlet of 5 rounds** = that environment's race tracks 1→5 (rounds may include tracks not yet\n758\topen in Race: Survival is their preview). Each round: you vs the **Ghost Guild** — Tex Mirage, Mlle Gravillon, Bobo\n759\tYeti — as ghost cars with name tags. Their runs are bot runs generated at round start (behind a 1-second \"WARMING UP\n760\tTHE GHOSTS\" card; deterministic per gauntlet + round): skills `base + 0.03·round + 0.02·rankIndex` with bases 0.78 /\n761\t0.86 / 0.93 and different seeds (Tex jittery-fast, Gravillon clean, Bobo late braker). Place by finish time (DNF after\n762\tthe last rival finishes + 15 s = last). **1st: +2 ranks, 2nd: +1, 3rd: stay, 4th: out.** Ranks: ROOKIE → DRIVER →\n763\tRACER → PILOT → ACE → MANIAC → CRACKMANIAC. Between rounds: standings card with portraits and a rival quip (§8.2).\n764\tClearing round 5 = \"GAUNTLET CLEARED\" + rewards. Best rank per gauntlet is recorded.\n765\t\n766\t### 5.6 Hot Seat and Split Screen (`modes/hotseat.js`, `modes/split.js`)\n767\t\n768\t**Hot Seat** (TrackMania 2003's local mode): 2–8 players (default names PLAYER 1…; letter wheel to rename), attempts\n769\tper turn 1/2/3, a cup of 1–5 tracks (pick or random). Turn order rotates per track. Before each turn a full-screen\n770\tcard \"PASS THE CONTROLLER TO {NAME}\" (Coco babbles; any button when ready). The leader's best run drives as a ghost.\n771\tScoring per track: 10-8-6-5-4-3-2-1 by best time; cup standings after each track; a podium at the end with each\n772\tplayer's car in their paint colour (assign 8 distinct colours).\n773\t\n774\t**Split Screen:** 2–4 players at once. Join screen: each pad presses ✕ or Options to join (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })`),\n775\tkeyboard players join with Enter (left half: WASD + F/G/H) or Numpad Enter (right half: arrows + . / ,), per the\n776\tengine's half-keyboard support. Layout `rows` for 2, `grid` for 3–4 (`game.splitScreen(n, { layout })`,\n777\t`world.addCamera()` per extra viewport; filters are off while split — engine rule). Same countdown; cars are ghosts to\n778\teach other (no collisions, TrackMania style). Each viewport has its own HUD; a player who finishes sees their place;\n779\tthe race ends when all finish or 30 s after the first finish. Best of 1 / 3 races.\n780\t\n781\t### 5.7 Online — AI Hub sessions (`modes/online.js`; protocol at `ai-hub/lib/hub/README.md`)\n782\t\n783\tMode **`ghost`**: each player runs their own copy of the round; positions are exchanged so each copy shows the others\n784\tas ghost cars; nothing they do affects your world. This *is* TrackMania online (cars never collide).\n785\t\n786\tHead metas (in the built HTML):\n787\t```html\n788\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n789\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n790\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n791\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n792\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Best lap time in 3 minutes wins: retry as often as you like\">\n793\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"R2/W gas, L2/S brake, stick/arrows steer, ○/Enter respawn, △/Delete restart\">\n794\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n795\t```\n796\tFlow when `AIHub.active` (true from the first line):\n797\t1. Skip title, attract and menus entirely. Boot, then `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4],\n798\t   card: true })`. If `info` is null, run the normal game.\n799\t2. Pick the round's track with `AIHub.rng('track')` from the session list **D1, D2, D3, R1, R2, S1, S2** (`info.round`\n800\t   advances the stream naturally); load it.\n801\t3. **Own card** (§ \"The card\" in the README): the track flyover looping, the track name, each player's name in their\n802\t   seat colour (`info.players[].color`: #e8443a, #3b82f6, #22c55e, #f5b700) with a READY tick from the `card` event's\n803\t   `ready` ids, the goal, the controls for this player's device, and the time left (`card.left`). Enter / ✕ / a tap →\n804\t   `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △ (button 3) or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. The card has no menus and draws no\n805\t   `Math.random` (use `AIHub.rng('card')` for any jitter). Call `AIHub.ready()` once the world is built — no key press.\n806\t4. On `start`, show 3-2-1-GO against `AIHub.time()` (play begins at 0). Then **time attack**: unlimited restarts and\n807\t   respawns; the round clock (3:00 from `AIHub.time() = 0`) shows top centre; your best time top right.\n808\t5. Every ~100 ms send `{ t: 'g', area: trackId, run: runCounter, ms, p: [x, y, z] (rounded 0.1 unit), q: [x, y, z, w]\n809\t   (4 decimals), v: kmh, f: flags }` with `AIHub.send(data, { reliable: false })` (≤ 10/s, well under the 20/s limit,\n810\t   < 200 bytes). On a new best, send `{ t: 'best', ms }` reliably. Receivers buffer 150 ms and interpolate; a ghost\n811\t   whose `area` differs is hidden; show name tags in seat colours (names drawn by the pixel font on canvas — never as\n812\t   HTML).\n813\t6. Each second `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`: with a best, `score = 2e6 − bestMs`, label `BEST 0:42.31`; without,\n814\t   `score = cpsThisRun·1000 + metresAlongRoute`, label `CP 2/3`.\n815\t7. At 3:00 by `AIHub.time()` — or at once on `time-up` — call `AIHub.result({ time: bestMs })` if you have a finish,\n816\t   else `AIHub.result({ score })`, exactly once, then show \"WAITING FOR THE OTHERS\" with live ghosts. Include `stats:\n817\t   { Runs: n, Respawns: n }`.\n818\t8. On `end`: stop input and sound (`game.audio.mute(true)`, freeze), show the hub's standings line if given.\n819\t9. On `leave`: remove that ghost. If WebGL 2/WebGPU init fails: `AIHub.fail('3D graphics are not available')`.\n820\t10. In a session: no Quit to title, no title/attract/editor/garage, no `alert/confirm/prompt`, no `window.open`, no\n821\t    network except the hub; Options is ignored while Create (Pad8) is held.\n822\tThe Multiplayer menu outside the hub shows an **Online** tile that explains: \"Online races run in AI Hub sessions —\n823\topen CRACKMANIA from AI Hub with friends.\"\n824\t\n825\t### 5.8 Replays (`modes/replay.js`)\n826\t\n827\tFrom results (\"Replay\") or the Replays list (10 slots: track, time, car, date; delete with □). Viewer: the run's\n828\tghost drawn as a normal (opaque) car with its paint, the HUD's timer and CP splits replayed, camera modes **Chase / TV\n829\t/ Orbit** (R1 / C cycles), play/pause (✕ / Space), scrub (left stick or ←/→; hold for 4×), speed 0.25×–4× (L2/R2 or\n830\t−/=), restart (△ / Home), exit (○ / Esc), mouse: drag to orbit, wheel to zoom, click the timeline bar to seek.\n831\tCustom-track replays embed the track.\n832\t\n833\t### 5.9 Garage — paint shop (`modes/garage.js`)\n834\t\n835\tA small **workshop world** (a separate `E.World3D` with a text `level`: brick walls, a car lift, torches, shelves,\n836\tcrates, barrels, a tyre rack — core shapes plus a few custom ones) with a turntable. Pick car (locked cars show a\n837\tsilhouette and the unlock requirement), then: **Body colour**, **Accent colour** (24-swatch grids, plus HSV sliders),\n838\t**Pattern** (Solid, Twin Stripes, Side Stripe, Checker Roof, Flames, Lightning, Number Panel, Two-Tone), **Pattern\n839\tcolour**, **Number** (00–99, drawn on doors and roof with a 3×5 pixel digit font made of thin boxes), **Rims**\n840\t(6 colours), **Helmet colour**. Live preview spins; △ toggles \"lights on\". Saved per car; used in every mode, replays,\n841\thub ghosts (others see their seat colour, you see your paint).\n842\t\n843\t### 5.10 Dev Mode (`ui/dev.js`; pause menu → \"Dev Mode\")\n844\t\n845\tAn overlay panel (left 45% of the screen, game visible and paused, or running in slow motion if chosen) with three\n846\ttabs (L1/R1, Q/E, click):\n847\t- **TOOLS:** Teleport to next / previous checkpoint; Finish now (records the current time); Award medal (B/S/G/A);\n848\t  Unlock everything; +1000 coppers; Reset profile (asks); Bot drives (toggle, skill slider); Re-bake medals for this\n849\t  track; Time scale 0.25× / 0.5× / 1×; Frame step (while paused); Free camera (fly with sticks/WASD); Show probes\n850\t  (wheel rays, contact plane, normal, κ, slip); Show colliders (wireframe of collision triangles, pen bars); Show route\n851\t  and racing line; Show gates; Show FPS and draw stats (`renderer.info`); Jump to (any track / puzzle / gauntlet\n852\t  round / scene by deep link).\n853\t- **TUNING:** live sliders with a value readout and the default marked; ←/→ adjust (hold accelerates), □ resets the\n854\t  row, △ **Reset all to defaults**; mouse drags. Rows: gravity, adhesion, loop assist; for the current car: vtop, A0,\n855\t  brake, steer low/high, grip, drift grip, air yaw, ride, cd; surfaces: ice/dirt/sand/snow grip; boost Δv/accel/time;\n856\t  wall restitution; landing loss; camera distance/height/FOV/FOV-by-speed; medal ratios gold/silver/bronze; rival\n857\t  skill base/step; copper multiplier. Values live in `CFG` (session-only unless \"Keep tuning\" is on, then\n858\t  `E.store('crackmania:dev')`).\n859\t- **INFO:** car state (speed, grounded, surface, block, κ, slip, air time, boost), run (steps, CPs, respawns), track\n860\t  (id, blocks, author time, medal times), build version (`E.versionLabel()`), backend (`E.World3D.backend`).\n861\t\n862\t### 5.11 Attract mode (`attract/attract.js`)\n863\t\n864\tOn the **title and every front-end menu screen** (not the editor, garage, settings or pause), 10 s without any input\n865\t(keys, mouse movement/clicks, pad buttons or stick past the dead zone) starts the attract loop; **any input** returns to\n866\tthe title (the input is consumed). A \"DEMO — PRESS ANY BUTTON\" banner pulses at the bottom; the CRACKMANIA logo sits\n867\tsmall in a corner. Segments (each with a caption card; ~100 s total, then loops):\n868\t1. **Race** — D5 \"The Big Crack\", bot with cheats, chase cam with TV-cam cuts at the loops and the canyon jump (25 s).\n869\t2. **Build** — a time-lapse of R1 being built: blocks drop in one by one with the bounce tween, the camera orbits,\n870\t   coppers tick down; then a 3-second test drive (15 s).\n871\t3. **Puzzle** — PS1 \"Icy Connect\": missing pieces fly into place, VALIDATE, a gold medal drops (15 s).\n872\t4. **Survival** — round on R2 vs the Ghost Guild; standings card with Tex's quip (20 s).\n873\t5. **Split screen** — two bots on S2, `rows` layout (15 s).\n874\t6. **Garage** — the three cars spin through paint jobs; the medal case (10 s).\n875\tThe bots may cheat freely (lane snap, perfect grip, instant respawn). Attract also runs on touch-only devices (§5.12).\n876\t\n877\t### 5.12 Touch-only devices and the About screen\n878\t\n879\t- **Touch-only gate** (`matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` true, `(any-pointer: fine)` false, no gamepad connected, no\n880\t  key pressed yet): the title shows the logo, a large **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a **SETTINGS** button\n881\t  (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). No touch controls anywhere (scenes declare `touch: []`; hide the engine's touch\n882\t  buttons). Attract mode runs after 10 s; a tap returns to the gate. A `gamepadconnected` event or any key press\n883\t  leaves the gate for the normal title.\n884\t- **About / Credits** (main menu → About): pages with large text: CRACKMANIA + version; **Source Information** (every\n885\t  field of TASK.md's list, filled from a `data/about.js` table the builder completes at the end — \"unknown\" where not\n886\t  confirmable); **Testing Feedback**, **Engine Feedback**, **Prompt Feedback** (the builder's answers, same as in the\n887\t  final reply and `exit-interview.json`); **Credits**: built on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT), three.js r182 (MIT), Rapier\n888\t  0.19.3 (Apache-2.0), AI Hub session client 1.4.0; any CC0 asset sets used (Kenney, KayKit); \"Inspired by TrackMania\n889\t  (2003) by Nadeo. CRACKMANIA is an original homage and is not affiliated with Nadeo or Ubisoft.\" The ending's credits\n890\t  roll reuses these pages with music.\n891\t\n892\t---\n893\t\n894\t## 6. Content\n895\t\n896\t### 6.1 The turtle format (how the shipped tracks are written)\n897\t\n898\tA track program is a start cell, a heading and a space-separated token list (`track/turtle.js` compiles it into\n899\tplacements; the editor's own format is the placement list, and both serialize the same way). The turtle stands in the\n900\tcell it will fill next, at level L (start 0), heading h.\n901\t\n902\t| Token | Places | Then |\n903\t| --- | --- | --- |\n904\t| `ST`, `CP`, `FN`, `BO`, `BU`, `KI` | that block in the current cell (KI also reserves L+1) | move 1 cell |\n905\t| `S`, `Sn`, `DS`, `DSn`, `IS`, `ISn`, `SN`, `SNn` | n straights (road / dirt / ice / snow road) | move n cells |\n906\t| `L1 R1 L2 R2 L3 R3`, `DL1 DR1 DL2 DR2`, `IL1 IR1 IL2 IR2`, `BL2 BR2` | the turn whose entry is the current cell (size n fills n×n) | to `c0 + (n−1)h + n·side`, heading = side |\n907\t| `U1 D1 U2 D2` | hill over 1 or 2 cells, spanning levels L..L+1 (U) or L−1..L (D) | move 1 or 2 cells, L ±1 |\n908\t| `LOOPR`, `LOOPL` | loop filling the 2×2 cells ahead/aside, levels L..L+3 | to `c0 + 2h + side`, heading unchanged |\n909\t| `CR` | crossing (may be entered again later from the side) | move 1 cell |\n910\t| `GAPn` | reserves n cells on L and L+1 (at L = 0: chasm cells, no base plate) | move n cells |\n911\t| `DROPn`, `RISEn` | nothing | L −n / +n (before a landing) |\n912\t| `LA` | landing (2 cells) at level L | move 2 cells |\n913\t\n914\tCompiler errors: out of the 32×32×16 grid, overlapping occupancy (except a `CR` crossed at right angles), no `ST` or\n915\t`FN`, a kicker with no landing within 5 cells ahead. The planning-time walker that checked every program below used\n916\texactly these rules (all pass, no overlaps); port it to `turtle.js` and keep it as a test.\n917\t\n918\t**Jump speeds** (G = 1.5 g, 15° lip, landing pad 2 cells long): `GAP1` needs ≈ 100 km/h at the lip, `GAP2` ≈ 150,\n919\t`GAP3` ≈ 185 on the same level; each `DROP` level lowers that by ~15–20 km/h. Every gap in the shipped tracks has a\n920\tboost pad or a long straight before it; the bot test fails a track whose speed plan can't make its gaps.\n921\t\n922\t### 6.2 Environments\n923\t\n924\t| | DUSTBOWL (desert) | HEDGEROW (countryside) | FROSTPEAK (alpine) |\n925\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n926\t| Tagline | Hot asphalt, big air | Tight lanes, loose gravel | Thin air, thin ice |\n927\t| Car | COYOTE — V8 muscle coupe, bouncy, drifty | PEBBLE — rally hatch, grippy, nimble | MOOSE — boxy 4x4, heavy, sure-footed on snow |\n928\t| Time of day | late afternoon, low warm sun from WSW, long shadows | bright midday | dusk alpenglow; headlights and street lamps on |\n929\t| Sky / fog | `#3a7fd8` → `#f6d29a`; fog `#f2d6a6` 600–1800 m | `#4aa0f0` → `#d8ecff`; fog `#d8ecff` 500–1500 m | `#2a5aa8` → `#f0d8e8`; fog `#e6eef8` 400–1300 m |\n930\t| Terrain outside the grid | dunes (`6·noise(x/80) + 3·noise(x/23)` m) and 6–8 flat-topped **mesas** 40–120 m tall, 300–900 m out, red/orange/cream strata | rolling hills (`25·noise/300 + 6·noise/60` m), patchwork fields (green / wheat / ploughed by a 60 m cell hash) with dark hedge lines, forest clumps, a far church spire | mountains rising to 400 m peaks at ~1.5 km (ridged noise), snow with blue shade, grey rock strata on steep slopes, pine forests near the grid |\n931\t| Base plate | sand ripples (`#e3b673`/`#d49a55`, pebble specks) | mown grass stripes (`#5a9a3a`/`#6aaa4a`, flower specks) | snow (`#eef3fa`, blue `#c8d6ea` shade, sparkle texels) |\n932\t| Accent (UI) | orange `#ff9a2a` | green `#6ad04a` | ice blue `#6ad8ff` |\n933\t| Boundary | striped concrete barriers | dry-stone wall | snow fence |\n934\t| Music | \"Heat Shimmer\" | \"Hedge Fund\" | \"Thin Ice\" |\n935\t\n936\tTerrain height inside the grid is −60 m (under the plate; seen only through chasms), rising to 0 at the grid edge.\n937\t\n938\t### 6.3 Race tracks (15) — programs validated on the 32×32 grid\n939\t\n940\tStart heading is E for all. Lengths are centreline estimates; the bot bakes the real author times. \"Teaches\" is what\n941\tthe track is for; the first-time tips (§8.2) fire on D1, D2, D3.\n942\t\n943\t| # | Name | Start | Program | ≈ m | CP | Teaches / signature |\n944\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n945\t| D1 | Sunburn Strip | (3,5) | `ST S2 BO S2 R2 S CP S2 L2 S2 U2 D2 S FN` | 731 | 1 | gas, steer, a boost, a checkpoint, a hill |\n946\t| D2 | Cactus Kicker | (2,4) | `ST S3 BO S KI GAP2 LA CP S R1 S2 L2 S2 BO S KI GAP2 LA S FN` | 933 | 1 | jumps over chasms; brake for the tight right |\n947\t| D3 | Looping Mesa | (2,3) | `ST S2 BO S2 LOOPR S CP S BR2 S2 U2 S2 D2 BR2 S BO S2 FN` | 998 | 1 | the loop; banked bends at full throttle |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"3ba8ecf3-f83f-4b8e-9fe1-8bd8499b4adb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:39:31.067Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work/PLAN.md","content":"\nRules: one Start (free), at least one Finish (free), any number of CPs; blocks can't overlap (3D occupancy) but can\nsit above others with ≥ 1 level of clearance (supports are generated automatically and never block a lane under\nthem); gaps under kickers are reserved automatically when a kicker is placed (shown hatched). A track is shareable\nand playable in Hot Seat / Split Screen once validated. A Dev Mode button \"Export as content\" prints a `data/tracks.js`\nentry (placements + metadata) — the designer workflow for growing the game later.\n\n### 5.5 Survival (`modes/survival.js`)\n\nPer environment a **gauntlet of 5 rounds** = that environment's race tracks 1→5 (rounds may include tracks not yet\nopen in Race: Survival is their preview). Each round: you vs the **Ghost Guild** — Tex Mirage, Mlle Gravillon, Bobo\nYeti — as ghost cars with name tags. Their runs are bot runs generated at round start (behind a 1-second \"WARMING UP\nTHE GHOSTS\" card; deterministic per gauntlet + round): skills `base + 0.03·round + 0.02·rankIndex` with bases 0.78 /\n0.86 / 0.93 and different seeds (Tex jittery-fast, Gravillon clean, Bobo late braker). Place by finish time (DNF after\nthe last rival finishes + 15 s = last). **1st: +2 ranks, 2nd: +1, 3rd: stay, 4th: out.** Ranks: ROOKIE → DRIVER →\nRACER → PILOT → ACE → MANIAC → CRACKMANIAC. Between rounds: standings card with portraits and a rival quip (§8.2).\nClearing round 5 = \"GAUNTLET CLEARED\" + rewards. Best rank per gauntlet is recorded.\n\n### 5.6 Hot Seat and Split Screen (`modes/hotseat.js`, `modes/split.js`)\n\n**Hot Seat** (TrackMania 2003's local mode): 2–8 players (default names PLAYER 1…; letter wheel to rename), attempts\nper turn 1/2/3, a cup of 1–5 tracks (pick or random). Turn order rotates per track. Before each turn a full-screen\ncard \"PASS THE CONTROLLER TO {NAME}\" (Coco babbles; any button when ready). The leader's best run drives as a ghost.\nScoring per track: 10-8-6-5-4-3-2-1 by best time; cup standings after each track; a podium at the end with each\nplayer's car in their paint colour (assign 8 distinct colours).\n\n**Split Screen:** 2–4 players at once. Join screen: each pad presses ✕ or Options to join (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })`),\nkeyboard players join with Enter (left half: WASD + F/G/H) or Numpad Enter (right half: arrows + . / ,), per the\nengine's half-keyboard support. Layout `rows` for 2, `grid` for 3–4 (`game.splitScreen(n, { layout })`,\n`world.addCamera()` per extra viewport; filters are off while split — engine rule). Same countdown; cars are ghosts to\neach other (no collisions, TrackMania style). Each viewport has its own HUD; a player who finishes sees their place;\nthe race ends when all finish or 30 s after the first finish. Best of 1 / 3 races.\n\n### 5.7 Online — AI Hub sessions (`modes/online.js`; protocol at `ai-hub/lib/hub/README.md`)\n\nMode **`ghost`**: each player runs their own copy of the round; positions are exchanged so each copy shows the others\nas ghost cars; nothing they do affects your world. This *is* TrackMania online (cars never collide).\n\nHead metas (in the built HTML):\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Best lap time in 3 minutes wins: retry as often as you like\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"R2/W gas, L2/S brake, stick/arrows steer, ○/Enter respawn, △/Delete restart\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n```\nFlow when `AIHub.active` (true from the first line):\n1. Skip title, attract and menus entirely. Boot, then `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4],\n   card: true })`. If `info` is null, run the normal game.\n2. Pick the round's track with `AIHub.rng('track')` from the session list **D1, D2, D3, R1, R2, S1, S2** (`info.round`\n   advances the stream naturally); load it.\n3. **Own card** (§ \"The card\" in the README): the track flyover looping, the track name, each player's name in their\n   seat colour (`info.players[].color`: #e8443a, #3b82f6, #22c55e, #f5b700) with a READY tick from the `card` event's\n   `ready` ids, the goal, the controls for this player's device, and the time left (`card.left`). Enter / ✕ / a tap →\n   `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △ (button 3) or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. The card has no menus and draws no\n   `Math.random` (use `AIHub.rng('card')` for any jitter). Call `AIHub.ready()` once the world is built — no key press.\n4. On `start`, show 3-2-1-GO against `AIHub.time()` (play begins at 0). Then **time attack**: unlimited restarts and\n   respawns; the round clock (3:00 from `AIHub.time() = 0`) shows top centre; your best time top right.\n5. Every ~100 ms send `{ t: 'g', area: trackId, run: runCounter, ms, p: [x, y, z] (rounded 0.1 unit), q: [x, y, z, w]\n   (4 decimals), v: kmh, f: flags }` with `AIHub.send(data, { reliable: false })` (≤ 10/s, well under the 20/s limit,\n   < 200 bytes). On a new best, send `{ t: 'best', ms }` reliably. Receivers buffer 150 ms and interpolate; a ghost\n   whose `area` differs is hidden; show name tags in seat colours (names drawn by the pixel font on canvas — never as\n   HTML).\n6. Each second `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`: with a best, `score = 2e6 − bestMs`, label `BEST 0:42.31`; without,\n   `score = cpsThisRun·1000 + metresAlongRoute`, label `CP 2/3`.\n7. At 3:00 by `AIHub.time()` — or at once on `time-up` — call `AIHub.result({ time: bestMs })` if you have a finish,\n   else `AIHub.result({ score })`, exactly once, then show \"WAITING FOR THE OTHERS\" with live ghosts. Include `stats:\n   { Runs: n, Respawns: n }`.\n8. On `end`: stop input and sound (`game.audio.mute(true)`, freeze), show the hub's standings line if given.\n9. On `leave`: remove that ghost. If WebGL 2/WebGPU init fails: `AIHub.fail('3D graphics are not available')`.\n10. In a session: no Quit to title, no title/attract/editor/garage, no `alert/confirm/prompt`, no `window.open`, no\n    network except the hub; Options is ignored while Create (Pad8) is held.\nThe Multiplayer menu outside the hub shows an **Online** tile that explains: \"Online races run in AI Hub sessions —\nopen CRACKMANIA from AI Hub with friends.\"\n\n### 5.8 Replays (`modes/replay.js`)\n\nFrom results (\"Replay\") or the Replays list (10 slots: track, time, car, date; delete with □). Viewer: the run's\nghost drawn as a normal (opaque) car with its paint, the HUD's timer and CP splits replayed, camera modes **Chase / TV\n/ Orbit** (R1 / C cycles), play/pause (✕ / Space), scrub (left stick or ←/→; hold for 4×), speed 0.25×–4× (L2/R2 or\n−/=), restart (△ / Home), exit (○ / Esc), mouse: drag to orbit, wheel to zoom, click the timeline bar to seek.\nCustom-track replays embed the track.\n\n### 5.9 Garage — paint shop (`modes/garage.js`)\n\nA small **workshop world** (a separate `E.World3D` with a text `level`: brick walls, a car lift, torches, shelves,\ncrates, barrels, a tyre rack — core shapes plus a few custom ones) with a turntable. Pick car (locked cars show a\nsilhouette and the unlock requirement), then: **Body colour**, **Accent colour** (24-swatch grids, plus HSV sliders),\n**Pattern** (Solid, Twin Stripes, Side Stripe, Checker Roof, Flames, Lightning, Number Panel, Two-Tone), **Pattern\ncolour**, **Number** (00–99, drawn on doors and roof with a 3×5 pixel digit font made of thin boxes), **Rims**\n(6 colours), **Helmet colour**. Live preview spins; △ toggles \"lights on\". Saved per car; used in every mode, replays,\nhub ghosts (others see their seat colour, you see your paint).\n\n### 5.10 Dev Mode (`ui/dev.js`; pause menu → \"Dev Mode\")\n\nAn overlay panel (left 45% of the screen, game visible and paused, or running in slow motion if chosen) with three\ntabs (L1/R1, Q/E, click):\n- **TOOLS:** Teleport to next / previous checkpoint; Finish now (records the current time); Award medal (B/S/G/A);\n  Unlock everything; +1000 coppers; Reset profile (asks); Bot drives (toggle, skill slider); Re-bake medals for this\n  track; Time scale 0.25× / 0.5× / 1×; Frame step (while paused); Free camera (fly with sticks/WASD); Show probes\n  (wheel rays, contact plane, normal, κ, slip); Show colliders (wireframe of collision triangles, pen bars); Show route\n  and racing line; Show gates; Show FPS and draw stats (`renderer.info`); Jump to (any track / puzzle / gauntlet\n  round / scene by deep link).\n- **TUNING:** live sliders with a value readout and the default marked; ←/→ adjust (hold accelerates), □ resets the\n  row, △ **Reset all to defaults**; mouse drags. Rows: gravity, adhesion, loop assist; for the current car: vtop, A0,\n  brake, steer low/high, grip, drift grip, air yaw, ride, cd; surfaces: ice/dirt/sand/snow grip; boost Δv/accel/time;\n  wall restitution; landing loss; camera distance/height/FOV/FOV-by-speed; medal ratios gold/silver/bronze; rival\n  skill base/step; copper multiplier. Values live in `CFG` (session-only unless \"Keep tuning\" is on, then\n  `E.store('crackmania:dev')`).\n- **INFO:** car state (speed, grounded, surface, block, κ, slip, air time, boost), run (steps, CPs, respawns), track\n  (id, blocks, author time, medal times), build version (`E.versionLabel()`), backend (`E.World3D.backend`).\n\n### 5.11 Attract mode (`attract/attract.js`)\n\nOn the **title and every front-end menu screen** (not the editor, garage, settings or pause), 10 s without any input\n(keys, mouse movement/clicks, pad buttons or stick past the dead zone) starts the attract loop; **any input** returns to\nthe title (the input is consumed). A \"DEMO — PRESS ANY BUTTON\" banner pulses at the bottom; the CRACKMANIA logo sits\nsmall in a corner. Segments (each with a caption card; ~100 s total, then loops):\n1. **Race** — D5 \"The Big Crack\", bot with cheats, chase cam with TV-cam cuts at the loops and the canyon jump (25 s).\n2. **Build** — a time-lapse of R1 being built: blocks drop in one by one with the bounce tween, the camera orbits,\n   coppers tick down; then a 3-second test drive (15 s).\n3. **Puzzle** — PS1 \"Icy Connect\": missing pieces fly into place, VALIDATE, a gold medal drops (15 s).\n4. **Survival** — round on R2 vs the Ghost Guild; standings card with Tex's quip (20 s).\n5. **Split screen** — two bots on S2, `rows` layout (15 s).\n6. **Garage** — the three cars spin through paint jobs; the medal case (10 s).\nThe bots may cheat freely (lane snap, perfect grip, instant respawn). Attract also runs on touch-only devices (§5.12).\n\n### 5.12 Touch-only devices and the About screen\n\n- **Touch-only gate** (`matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` true, `(any-pointer: fine)` false, no gamepad connected, no\n  key pressed yet): the title shows the logo, a large **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a **SETTINGS** button\n  (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). No touch controls anywhere (scenes declare `touch: []`; hide the engine's touch\n  buttons). Attract mode runs after 10 s; a tap returns to the gate. A `gamepadconnected` event or any key press\n  leaves the gate for the normal title.\n- **About / Credits** (main menu → About): pages with large text: CRACKMANIA + version; **Source Information** (every\n  field of TASK.md's list, filled from a `data/about.js` table the builder completes at the end — \"unknown\" where not\n  confirmable); **Testing Feedback**, **Engine Feedback**, **Prompt Feedback** (the builder's answers, same as in the\n  final reply and `exit-interview.json`); **Credits**: built on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT), three.js r182 (MIT), Rapier\n  0.19.3 (Apache-2.0), AI Hub session client 1.4.0; any CC0 asset sets used (Kenney, KayKit); \"Inspired by TrackMania\n  (2003) by Nadeo. CRACKMANIA is an original homage and is not affiliated with Nadeo or Ubisoft.\" The ending's credits\n  roll reuses these pages with music.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Content\n\n### 6.1 The turtle format (how the shipped tracks are written)\n\nA track program is a start cell, a heading and a space-separated token list (`track/turtle.js` compiles it into\nplacements; the editor's own format is the placement list, and both serialize the same way). The turtle stands in the\ncell it will fill next, at level L (start 0), heading h.\n\n| Token | Places | Then |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `ST`, `CP`, `FN`, `BO`, `BU`, `KI` | that block in the current cell (KI also reserves L+1) | move 1 cell |\n| `S`, `Sn`, `DS`, `DSn`, `IS`, `ISn`, `SN`, `SNn` | n straights (road / dirt / ice / snow road) | move n cells |\n| `L1 R1 L2 R2 L3 R3`, `DL1 DR1 DL2 DR2`, `IL1 IR1 IL2 IR2`, `BL2 BR2` | the turn whose entry is the current cell (size n fills n×n) | to `c0 + (n−1)h + n·side`, heading = side |\n| `U1 D1 U2 D2` | hill over 1 or 2 cells, spanning levels L..L+1 (U) or L−1..L (D) | move 1 or 2 cells, L ±1 |\n| `LOOPR`, `LOOPL` | loop filling the 2×2 cells ahead/aside, levels L..L+3 | to `c0 + 2h + side`, heading unchanged |\n| `CR` | crossing (may be entered again later from the side) | move 1 cell |\n| `GAPn` | reserves n cells on L and L+1 (at L = 0: chasm cells, no base plate) | move n cells |\n| `DROPn`, `RISEn` | nothing | L −n / +n (before a landing) |\n| `LA` | landing (2 cells) at level L | move 2 cells |\n\nCompiler errors: out of the 32×32×16 grid, overlapping occupancy (except a `CR` crossed at right angles), no `ST` or\n`FN`, a kicker with no landing within 5 cells ahead. The planning-time walker that checked every program below used\nexactly these rules (all pass, no overlaps); port it to `turtle.js` and keep it as a test.\n\n**Jump speeds** (G = 1.5 g, 15° lip, landing pad 2 cells long): `GAP1` needs ≈ 100 km/h at the lip, `GAP2` ≈ 150,\n`GAP3` ≈ 185 on the same level; each `DROP` level lowers that by ~15–20 km/h. Every gap in the shipped tracks has a\nboost pad or a long straight before it; the bot test fails a track whose speed plan can't make its gaps.\n\n### 6.2 Environments\n\n| | DUSTBOWL (desert) | HEDGEROW (countryside) | FROSTPEAK (alpine) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Tagline | Hot asphalt, big air | Tight lanes, loose gravel | Thin air, thin ice |\n| Car | COYOTE — V8 muscle coupe, bouncy, drifty | PEBBLE — rally hatch, grippy, nimble | MOOSE — boxy 4x4, heavy, sure-footed on snow |\n| Time of day | late afternoon, low warm sun from WSW, long shadows | bright midday | dusk alpenglow; headlights and street lamps on |\n| Sky / fog | `#3a7fd8` → `#f6d29a`; fog `#f2d6a6` 600–1800 m | `#4aa0f0` → `#d8ecff`; fog `#d8ecff` 500–1500 m | `#2a5aa8` → `#f0d8e8`; fog `#e6eef8` 400–1300 m |\n| Terrain outside the grid | dunes (`6·noise(x/80) + 3·noise(x/23)` m) and 6–8 flat-topped **mesas** 40–120 m tall, 300–900 m out, red/orange/cream strata | rolling hills (`25·noise/300 + 6·noise/60` m), patchwork fields (green / wheat / ploughed by a 60 m cell hash) with dark hedge lines, forest clumps, a far church spire | mountains rising to 400 m peaks at ~1.5 km (ridged noise), snow with blue shade, grey rock strata on steep slopes, pine forests near the grid |\n| Base plate | sand ripples (`#e3b673`/`#d49a55`, pebble specks) | mown grass stripes (`#5a9a3a`/`#6aaa4a`, flower specks) | snow (`#eef3fa`, blue `#c8d6ea` shade, sparkle texels) |\n| Accent (UI) | orange `#ff9a2a` | green `#6ad04a` | ice blue `#6ad8ff` |\n| Boundary | striped concrete barriers | dry-stone wall | snow fence |\n| Music | \"Heat Shimmer\" | \"Hedge Fund\" | \"Thin Ice\" |\n\nTerrain height inside the grid is −60 m (under the plate; seen only through chasms), rising to 0 at the grid edge.\n\n### 6.3 Race tracks (15) — programs validated on the 32×32 grid\n\nStart heading is E for all. Lengths are centreline estimates; the bot bakes the real author times. \"Teaches\" is what\nthe track is for; the first-time tips (§8.2) fire on D1, D2, D3.\n\n| # | Name | Start | Program | ≈ m | CP | Teaches / signature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| D1 | Sunburn Strip | (3,5) | `ST S2 BO S2 R2 S CP S2 L2 S2 U2 D2 S FN` | 731 | 1 | gas, steer, a boost, a checkpoint, a hill |\n| D2 | Cactus Kicker | (2,4) | `ST S3 BO S KI GAP2 LA CP S R1 S2 L2 S2 BO S KI GAP2 LA S FN` | 933 | 1 | jumps over chasms; brake for the tight right |\n| D3 | Looping Mesa | (2,3) | `ST S2 BO S2 LOOPR S CP S BR2 S2 U2 S2 D2 BR2 S BO S2 FN` | 998 | 1 | the loop; banked bends at full throttle |","numLines":200,"startLine":748,"totalLines":1416}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GSf9C3AJAgegUizacAMkhD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
