{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh325Gjqb4usZeQqwbGz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YTinVGpZu6DerUysT2xsSX","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work/PLAN.md","offset":975,"limit":135},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1093,"cache_read_input_tokens":527941,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1093},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"4a0f9505-9599-45db-8c56-dee2d314cdf1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:40:12.288Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3251N1qN4f32JZtNQe","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YTinVGpZu6DerUysT2xsSX":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work/PLAN.md","offset":975,"limit":135}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YTinVGpZu6DerUysT2xsSX","type":"tool_result","content":"975\t### 6.4 Puzzles (6) — fixed blocks and inventories computed from validated solutions\n976\t\n977\tCoordinates are (cx, cy, level, heading). \"Solution\" is the reference route (it also bakes the medal times); the\n978\t**inventory** is the solution's pieces plus extras. The player may find other routes inside the build zone.\n979\t\n980\t| # | Env | Name | Fixed | Build zone (x, y, levels) | No-build cells | Solution | Inventory |\n981\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n982\t| PD1 | Dustbowl | Missing Bend | ST (4,8,0,E), CP (8,11,0,S), FN (11,14,0,E) | 2–14, 6–16, 0–1 | rocks at (6,10), (10,9), (9,15) | `ST S2 R2 S CP S L2 S FN` | S×6, R2, L2, R1, L1, BO |\n983\t| PD2 | Dustbowl | Mind the Gap | ST (3,6,0,E), CP (13,6,0,E), FN (15,8,0,S) | 1–17, 2–11, 0–1 | **canyon**: all cells x = 8–9, y = 2–11 | `ST S BO S KI GAP2 LA S CP S R1 S FN` | S×6, BO, KI, LA, R1, R2 |\n984\t| PR1 | Hedgerow | Hedge Maze | ST (3,3,0,E), CP (7,5,0,E), FN (11,7,0,E) | 2–12, 2–9, 0–1 | hedges at (4,4), (4,5), (6,3), (7,3), (8,3), (6,6), (7,6), (7,7), (8,7), (11,5), (11,6) | `ST S DR1 DS DL1 S CP S R1 S L1 S FN` | S×7, DS×2, DR1, DL1, R1, L1, R2 |\n985\t| PR2 | Hedgerow | Over and Under | ST (4,12,0,E), CP (4,14,0,S), FN (4,16,0,S) | 2–10, 6–18, 0–2 | pond at (7,14), (8,14) | `ST S2 L2 S L2 S L2 U1 S2 D1 CP S FN` | S×8, L2×3, U1, D1, R1, L1 |\n986\t| PS1 | Frostpeak | Icy Connect | ST (3,5,0,E), CP (7,8,0,S), FN (11,11,0,E) | 2–13, 3–13, 0–1 | rocks at (5,9), (9,6) | `ST S IS R2 S CP S L2 IS S FN` | S×4, IS×3, R2, L2, R1, L1 |\n987\t| PS2 | Frostpeak | Summit Puzzle | ST (3,8,0,E), CP (11,8,2,E), FN (13,16,0,S) | 2–15, 6–18, 0–3 | pines at (8,12), (10,14) | `ST S U2 S U2 S CP R2 S KI GAP1 DROP2 LA S FN` | S×6, U2×2, D2×2, R2, KI, LA, BO |\n988\t\n989\tPR2 forces a bridge (the CP lies straight south of the start, so the route must pass over the start straight).\n990\tPD2's canyon forces the kicker. PS2 can be solved slowly with D2×2 or fast with the kicker. Tests place each solution\n991\tthrough the editor API and validate it with the bot.\n992\t\n993\t### 6.5 Survival gauntlets\n994\t\n995\tDUSTBOWL GAUNTLET = D1→D5, HEDGEROW GAUNTLET = R1→R5, FROSTPEAK GAUNTLET = S1→S5; rivals per §5.5.\n996\t\n997\t### 6.6 Scenery and trackside dressing (`track/deco.js`, seeded by track id)\n998\t\n999\tCandidates: grid cells with no track piece at any level, no reserved air, no chasm, at least 4 m from any road edge.\n1000\tFill rates and mixes:\n1001\t- **Dustbowl** 35% of candidates: saguaro cactus 40%, barrel-cactus cluster 20%, rocks 20%, rolling tumbleweed 5%,\n1002\t  oil pumpjack 5% (≥ 2 cells from road), billboard 10% (only beside straights, facing the road).\n1003\t- **Hedgerow** 50%: trees 35%, bushes 20%, hay bales 15%, fences along verges 10%, cows 5%, barn or farmhouse 5%\n1004\t  (needs a free 2×2), windmill 2%.\n1005\t- **Frostpeak** 45%: snowy pines 55%, rocks 15%, chalets 8%, snowmen 5%, ice blocks 5%, one ski-lift pylon line if\n1006\t  a free row of 6 cells exists.\n1007\tAlways: a **chevron sign** on the outside of every tight turn (R1/L1, DL1/DR1, IL1/IR1) and of any turn the bot's speed\n1008\tplan enters above 150 km/h (readability at 240 px tall); tyre stacks (Dustbowl) / hay bales (Hedgerow) / snowbanks\n1009\t(Frostpeak) on the outside of turns; two grandstands with a waving crowd near start and finish; Monsieur Drapeau beside\n1010\tthe start gate; banners on checkpoint gates. Props are solid: simple colliders (cylinders r 0.4–0.8 m for trunks and\n1011\tcacti, boxes for buildings and billboard posts).\n1012\t\n1013\t---\n1014\t\n1015\t## 7. Art direction and animation\n1016\t\n1017\t### 7.1 The look\n1018\t\n1019\tThe engine's native 3D style is the base: the game's own low resolution (`World3D.SETTINGS` \"3D picture: Pixels\" by\n1020\tdefault; Balanced/Full selectable), toon bands, ink outlines on pen parts, crisp nearest-filtered textures, sun with\n1021\tshadows, fog to the horizon, the filter setting (None / Comic cel / Pixel) left to the player. Design for 240 px tall:\n1022\tbig shapes, high-contrast curbs and edge lines, chevron boards before tight turns, saturated gates. Colour script:\n1023\tDustbowl warm oranges/teal sky; Hedgerow greens/yellows/white; Frostpeak whites/blues with pink sky and warm lamps.\n1024\tTASK.md treats performance as unlimited: dress scenes generously (sun shadows on, dense scenery, crowds, animated\n1025\tprops, lamps) — but still never create materials after boot.\n1026\t\n1027\t### 7.2 Textures (`env/textures.js`; bake with `E.mkCanvas(w, h)` → `THREE.CanvasTexture`, NearestFilter, repeat)\n1028\t\n1029\t64×64 or 128×128 px tiles drawn pixel by pixel with `E.tones()` ramps and `E.hash2`/`E.noise2` speckle: asphalt (dark\n1030\tgrey, aggregate speckles, faint cracks, white edge lines and a yellow dashed centre at the right texel columns),\n1031\ttarmac (lighter, patched), dirt (ruts, pebbles), packed snow road (blue-white with tyre tracks), ice (blue, white\n1032\tstreaks), red/white and blue/white curb stripes (1 m period), boost chevrons (separate emissive overlay), sand ripples,\n1033\tmown grass stripes, snow with sparkle texels, concrete (pillars, barriers with orange/white stripes), earth embankment,\n1034\trock strata (terrain colour function: bands by height with noise), stone wall, steel rail.\n1035\t\n1036\t### 7.3 Cars (`car/draw.js`, the pen, frame from E1; 25–45 parts each, outlines automatic)\n1037\t\n1038\tDraw at the interpolated pose (`game.alpha`). Body pitch/roll lean from acceleration (≤ 4°, smoothed) on top of the\n1039\tphysics frame; each wheel at its probe's compression (spring-smoothed, so landings squash), spinning with speed, front\n1040\twheels turned by the steer angle; brake lights glow (pen `glow`) while braking; headlights in Frostpeak; exhaust puffs\n1041\tat idle and a flame + glow while boosting; a helmet (ball + visor) visible through the windscreen.\n1042\t- **Coyote:** long low body box, raised hood with a scoop, fastback cabin with dark glass slabs, chrome bumpers,\n1043\t  side exhausts (tubes), wide rear tyres, twin stripes by default.\n1044\t- **Pebble:** short tall hatch, big roof vent, rally wing, mud flaps, four-lamp light pod on the bonnet, diagonal\n1045\t  livery slab by default.\n1046\t- **Moose:** tall boxy 4x4, roll bar, roof rack with lamps, spare wheel on the tailgate, snorkel, knobbly big wheels.\n1047\tPaint system: `primary`, `accent`, `pattern` (8, §5.9) as extra thin boxes/slabs on top of the body (stripes, checker\n1048\tsquares, flame wedges via `slab`, lightning zig-zag), `number` from a 3×5 digit font of tiny boxes on doors and roof,\n1049\t`rims`, `helmet`. Ghosts draw the same parts with `pen.ghost = true` (E3) tinted toward white.\n1050\t\n1051\t### 7.4 Characters and props\n1052\t\n1053\tCharacters are `E.Humanoid` rigs (the engine's animation system: poses, moves, `drawPortrait` for dialogs):\n1054\t- **Coco Asphalte** — `build: 'heroic'`, hard hat (`hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#ffd030' }`), ponytail, orange\n1055\t  hi-vis coat with reflective trim, clipboard held (pen in hand via `rig.hand()` in 3D scenes); portrait in dialogs.\n1056\t- **Monsieur Drapeau** — chibi build, cap, white shirt, black trousers; holds a chequered flag (pen-drawn on `rig.hand()`);\n1057\t  idle sway, raises the flag at \"3\", drops it on GO (pose + custom arm offset), cheers at your finish.\n1058\t- **Ghost Guild** — Tex Mirage (`hat: 'cap'` styled as a cowboy hat in tan, poncho cape), Mlle Gravillon (goggles via\n1059\t  `hat: 'band'`, racing jacket), Bobo Yeti (`build: 'bulky'`, white `hood`, fur colours). Portraits on Survival cards;\n1060\t  their ghost cars in their colours (Tex orange, Gravillon violet, Bobo white).\n1061\t- **Crowd** — `style: 'classic'` humanoids (cheap) on the grandstands, `wave`/`cheer` poses on a stagger, louder\n1062\t  cheering when you pass a gate or finish.\n1063\t- **Driver** — your helmeted driver on the results podium (`pose: 'cheer'`) beside the car.\n1064\t\n1065\tProps: use the engine's core shapes and store sets where they fit (`tree`, `pine` (snow material), `bush`, `rock`,\n1066\t`fence`, `barrel`, `crate`, `sign`, `lamppost`; `kenney-graveyard:hay-bale`, `kenney-holiday:snowman`,\n1067\t`kenney-holiday:cabin-fence`, `kenney-nature:log-large`, `kenney-pirate:palm-detailed-straight` for the Dustbowl\n1068\toasis; cut only the entries used into a set of your own with `tools/asset-set.mjs`). **New shapes** (asset entries per\n1069\t`docs/ASSETS.md`, checked with `tools/asset-sheet.mjs`): saguaro cactus (3 variants), barrel-cactus cluster, mesa\n1070\trock arch, billboard frame (the poster drawn by the pen: \"COPPER COLA\", \"LOOP INSURANCE\", \"COCO ASPHALTE BUILDS\n1071\tTRACKS\"), grandstand, tyre stack, traffic cone, chevron sign board, barn, farmhouse, chalet, stone-wall segment, ski-lift\n1072\tpylon, snow pole, ice block, igloo, workshop car lift. **Moving props drawn by the pen each frame:** pumpjack (rocking\n1073\tbeam), Dustbowl water-pump windmill and Hedgerow windmill (turning blades), tumbleweeds (rolling, bouncing), cows\n1074\t(grazing head bob, tail swish; ball/box/tube parts), ski-lift chairs (moving on the cable), flags on poles (waving),\n1075\tgate flip-digit boards (your current time and checkpoint split flip in), start lights (5 red → green), finish confetti\n1076\tcannons, boost chevrons (lit in sequence).\n1077\t\n1078\t### 7.5 Effects (game.particles in 3D, the pen, the camera)\n1079\t\n1080\tDust plumes by surface (sand/dirt/snow colours) from the rear wheels ∝ speed and slide; tyre smoke on asphalt slides;\n1081\tskid marks (dark thin pen slabs on the road, last 200, fading over 8 s); sparks on wall scrapes (`particles.sparks`)\n1082\tand on hard landings with the chassis; landing dust ring (`particles.ring`); boost: exhaust flame glows, a speed-line\n1083\toverlay, FOV kick, chevron flash; checkpoint: gate ring flash + `glints`; respawn: glints + scale-in; finish: confetti\n1084\t(`bits` in env colours), fireworks over the stands after a medal; splash at the mill pond; snow puffs off pine\n1085\tbranches when you pass close. Screen shake and flashes follow the engine's comfort settings.\n1086\t\n1087\t### 7.6 UI art (pixel sprites via `E.sprite`, `E.font`, `E.ui`)\n1088\t\n1089\tLogo: `E.font.title('CRACKMANIA', …, { scale: 4, colors: ['#fff6d0', '#ffd060', '#ff8a2a', '#c8402a'], depth: 3 })`\n1090\twith animated crack lines (pen-free 2D `px.line` zig-zags growing across the letters, then a puff of asphalt bits).\n1091\tMedal icons B/S/G/A (16 px discs with ribbon and letter), copper coin, flag, lock, env emblems (cactus, cabbage,\n1092\tsnowflake), car silhouettes, chunky timer digits (9×14 px, outlined), **controller glyphs**: PlayStation (✕ ○ □ △ in\n1093\ttheir shapes and colours, L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, Create, sticks, d-pad), Xbox (A B X Y in coloured circles, LB RB LT\n1094\tRT, Menu, View), keyboard keycaps (letter or word), mouse (left/right/wheel). Panels: `E.ui.box` with a dark\n1095\ttranslucent gradient and the environment accent border.\n1096\t\n1097\t### 7.7 Animation list (everything that moves, built on the engine's rigs, tweens and scripts)\n1098\t\n1099\tCar: suspension, lean, wheel spin and steer, brake/head lights, boost flames, landing squash, flop roll-over, respawn\n1100\tscale-in, finish slow-motion. Camera: flyover intro, chase lag, FOV with speed, TV cuts, finish orbit. Characters:\n1101\tCoco's dialog gestures (pose changes per line among the engine's poses `wave`, `hips`, `cheer`, `cast`, plus\n1102\t`point: true` to point) and portrait expressions (`expr: 'smile' | 'shout'`), Drapeau's flag routine, the crowd, the podium cheer, Survival rivals' portraits reacting (smile when ahead,\n1103\twince when beaten). World: windmills, pumpjack, cows, tumbleweeds, ski-lift, flags, start lights, flip boards,\n1104\tconfetti, fireworks. UI: tile focus scale, medal drop-in (outBack) and shine sweep, coppers count-up with coin ticks,\n1105\tpalette slide, block drop-in with bounce in the editor and the attract build time-lapse, logo crack, unlock \"stamp\".\n1106\t\n1107\t---\n1108\t\n1109\t## 8. Audio, story and text"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"c92ed278-749e-4b0c-be0b-2b888a61f51c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:40:12.294Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 6.4 Puzzles (6) — fixed blocks and inventories computed from validated solutions\n\nCoordinates are (cx, cy, level, heading). \"Solution\" is the reference route (it also bakes the medal times); the\n**inventory** is the solution's pieces plus extras. The player may find other routes inside the build zone.\n\n| # | Env | Name | Fixed | Build zone (x, y, levels) | No-build cells | Solution | Inventory |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| PD1 | Dustbowl | Missing Bend | ST (4,8,0,E), CP (8,11,0,S), FN (11,14,0,E) | 2–14, 6–16, 0–1 | rocks at (6,10), (10,9), (9,15) | `ST S2 R2 S CP S L2 S FN` | S×6, R2, L2, R1, L1, BO |\n| PD2 | Dustbowl | Mind the Gap | ST (3,6,0,E), CP (13,6,0,E), FN (15,8,0,S) | 1–17, 2–11, 0–1 | **canyon**: all cells x = 8–9, y = 2–11 | `ST S BO S KI GAP2 LA S CP S R1 S FN` | S×6, BO, KI, LA, R1, R2 |\n| PR1 | Hedgerow | Hedge Maze | ST (3,3,0,E), CP (7,5,0,E), FN (11,7,0,E) | 2–12, 2–9, 0–1 | hedges at (4,4), (4,5), (6,3), (7,3), (8,3), (6,6), (7,6), (7,7), (8,7), (11,5), (11,6) | `ST S DR1 DS DL1 S CP S R1 S L1 S FN` | S×7, DS×2, DR1, DL1, R1, L1, R2 |\n| PR2 | Hedgerow | Over and Under | ST (4,12,0,E), CP (4,14,0,S), FN (4,16,0,S) | 2–10, 6–18, 0–2 | pond at (7,14), (8,14) | `ST S2 L2 S L2 S L2 U1 S2 D1 CP S FN` | S×8, L2×3, U1, D1, R1, L1 |\n| PS1 | Frostpeak | Icy Connect | ST (3,5,0,E), CP (7,8,0,S), FN (11,11,0,E) | 2–13, 3–13, 0–1 | rocks at (5,9), (9,6) | `ST S IS R2 S CP S L2 IS S FN` | S×4, IS×3, R2, L2, R1, L1 |\n| PS2 | Frostpeak | Summit Puzzle | ST (3,8,0,E), CP (11,8,2,E), FN (13,16,0,S) | 2–15, 6–18, 0–3 | pines at (8,12), (10,14) | `ST S U2 S U2 S CP R2 S KI GAP1 DROP2 LA S FN` | S×6, U2×2, D2×2, R2, KI, LA, BO |\n\nPR2 forces a bridge (the CP lies straight south of the start, so the route must pass over the start straight).\nPD2's canyon forces the kicker. PS2 can be solved slowly with D2×2 or fast with the kicker. Tests place each solution\nthrough the editor API and validate it with the bot.\n\n### 6.5 Survival gauntlets\n\nDUSTBOWL GAUNTLET = D1→D5, HEDGEROW GAUNTLET = R1→R5, FROSTPEAK GAUNTLET = S1→S5; rivals per §5.5.\n\n### 6.6 Scenery and trackside dressing (`track/deco.js`, seeded by track id)\n\nCandidates: grid cells with no track piece at any level, no reserved air, no chasm, at least 4 m from any road edge.\nFill rates and mixes:\n- **Dustbowl** 35% of candidates: saguaro cactus 40%, barrel-cactus cluster 20%, rocks 20%, rolling tumbleweed 5%,\n  oil pumpjack 5% (≥ 2 cells from road), billboard 10% (only beside straights, facing the road).\n- **Hedgerow** 50%: trees 35%, bushes 20%, hay bales 15%, fences along verges 10%, cows 5%, barn or farmhouse 5%\n  (needs a free 2×2), windmill 2%.\n- **Frostpeak** 45%: snowy pines 55%, rocks 15%, chalets 8%, snowmen 5%, ice blocks 5%, one ski-lift pylon line if\n  a free row of 6 cells exists.\nAlways: a **chevron sign** on the outside of every tight turn (R1/L1, DL1/DR1, IL1/IR1) and of any turn the bot's speed\nplan enters above 150 km/h (readability at 240 px tall); tyre stacks (Dustbowl) / hay bales (Hedgerow) / snowbanks\n(Frostpeak) on the outside of turns; two grandstands with a waving crowd near start and finish; Monsieur Drapeau beside\nthe start gate; banners on checkpoint gates. Props are solid: simple colliders (cylinders r 0.4–0.8 m for trunks and\ncacti, boxes for buildings and billboard posts).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Art direction and animation\n\n### 7.1 The look\n\nThe engine's native 3D style is the base: the game's own low resolution (`World3D.SETTINGS` \"3D picture: Pixels\" by\ndefault; Balanced/Full selectable), toon bands, ink outlines on pen parts, crisp nearest-filtered textures, sun with\nshadows, fog to the horizon, the filter setting (None / Comic cel / Pixel) left to the player. Design for 240 px tall:\nbig shapes, high-contrast curbs and edge lines, chevron boards before tight turns, saturated gates. Colour script:\nDustbowl warm oranges/teal sky; Hedgerow greens/yellows/white; Frostpeak whites/blues with pink sky and warm lamps.\nTASK.md treats performance as unlimited: dress scenes generously (sun shadows on, dense scenery, crowds, animated\nprops, lamps) — but still never create materials after boot.\n\n### 7.2 Textures (`env/textures.js`; bake with `E.mkCanvas(w, h)` → `THREE.CanvasTexture`, NearestFilter, repeat)\n\n64×64 or 128×128 px tiles drawn pixel by pixel with `E.tones()` ramps and `E.hash2`/`E.noise2` speckle: asphalt (dark\ngrey, aggregate speckles, faint cracks, white edge lines and a yellow dashed centre at the right texel columns),\ntarmac (lighter, patched), dirt (ruts, pebbles), packed snow road (blue-white with tyre tracks), ice (blue, white\nstreaks), red/white and blue/white curb stripes (1 m period), boost chevrons (separate emissive overlay), sand ripples,\nmown grass stripes, snow with sparkle texels, concrete (pillars, barriers with orange/white stripes), earth embankment,\nrock strata (terrain colour function: bands by height with noise), stone wall, steel rail.\n\n### 7.3 Cars (`car/draw.js`, the pen, frame from E1; 25–45 parts each, outlines automatic)\n\nDraw at the interpolated pose (`game.alpha`). Body pitch/roll lean from acceleration (≤ 4°, smoothed) on top of the\nphysics frame; each wheel at its probe's compression (spring-smoothed, so landings squash), spinning with speed, front\nwheels turned by the steer angle; brake lights glow (pen `glow`) while braking; headlights in Frostpeak; exhaust puffs\nat idle and a flame + glow while boosting; a helmet (ball + visor) visible through the windscreen.\n- **Coyote:** long low body box, raised hood with a scoop, fastback cabin with dark glass slabs, chrome bumpers,\n  side exhausts (tubes), wide rear tyres, twin stripes by default.\n- **Pebble:** short tall hatch, big roof vent, rally wing, mud flaps, four-lamp light pod on the bonnet, diagonal\n  livery slab by default.\n- **Moose:** tall boxy 4x4, roll bar, roof rack with lamps, spare wheel on the tailgate, snorkel, knobbly big wheels.\nPaint system: `primary`, `accent`, `pattern` (8, §5.9) as extra thin boxes/slabs on top of the body (stripes, checker\nsquares, flame wedges via `slab`, lightning zig-zag), `number` from a 3×5 digit font of tiny boxes on doors and roof,\n`rims`, `helmet`. Ghosts draw the same parts with `pen.ghost = true` (E3) tinted toward white.\n\n### 7.4 Characters and props\n\nCharacters are `E.Humanoid` rigs (the engine's animation system: poses, moves, `drawPortrait` for dialogs):\n- **Coco Asphalte** — `build: 'heroic'`, hard hat (`hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#ffd030' }`), ponytail, orange\n  hi-vis coat with reflective trim, clipboard held (pen in hand via `rig.hand()` in 3D scenes); portrait in dialogs.\n- **Monsieur Drapeau** — chibi build, cap, white shirt, black trousers; holds a chequered flag (pen-drawn on `rig.hand()`);\n  idle sway, raises the flag at \"3\", drops it on GO (pose + custom arm offset), cheers at your finish.\n- **Ghost Guild** — Tex Mirage (`hat: 'cap'` styled as a cowboy hat in tan, poncho cape), Mlle Gravillon (goggles via\n  `hat: 'band'`, racing jacket), Bobo Yeti (`build: 'bulky'`, white `hood`, fur colours). Portraits on Survival cards;\n  their ghost cars in their colours (Tex orange, Gravillon violet, Bobo white).\n- **Crowd** — `style: 'classic'` humanoids (cheap) on the grandstands, `wave`/`cheer` poses on a stagger, louder\n  cheering when you pass a gate or finish.\n- **Driver** — your helmeted driver on the results podium (`pose: 'cheer'`) beside the car.\n\nProps: use the engine's core shapes and store sets where they fit (`tree`, `pine` (snow material), `bush`, `rock`,\n`fence`, `barrel`, `crate`, `sign`, `lamppost`; `kenney-graveyard:hay-bale`, `kenney-holiday:snowman`,\n`kenney-holiday:cabin-fence`, `kenney-nature:log-large`, `kenney-pirate:palm-detailed-straight` for the Dustbowl\noasis; cut only the entries used into a set of your own with `tools/asset-set.mjs`). **New shapes** (asset entries per\n`docs/ASSETS.md`, checked with `tools/asset-sheet.mjs`): saguaro cactus (3 variants), barrel-cactus cluster, mesa\nrock arch, billboard frame (the poster drawn by the pen: \"COPPER COLA\", \"LOOP INSURANCE\", \"COCO ASPHALTE BUILDS\nTRACKS\"), grandstand, tyre stack, traffic cone, chevron sign board, barn, farmhouse, chalet, stone-wall segment, ski-lift\npylon, snow pole, ice block, igloo, workshop car lift. **Moving props drawn by the pen each frame:** pumpjack (rocking\nbeam), Dustbowl water-pump windmill and Hedgerow windmill (turning blades), tumbleweeds (rolling, bouncing), cows\n(grazing head bob, tail swish; ball/box/tube parts), ski-lift chairs (moving on the cable), flags on poles (waving),\ngate flip-digit boards (your current time and checkpoint split flip in), start lights (5 red → green), finish confetti\ncannons, boost chevrons (lit in sequence).\n\n### 7.5 Effects (game.particles in 3D, the pen, the camera)\n\nDust plumes by surface (sand/dirt/snow colours) from the rear wheels ∝ speed and slide; tyre smoke on asphalt slides;\nskid marks (dark thin pen slabs on the road, last 200, fading over 8 s); sparks on wall scrapes (`particles.sparks`)\nand on hard landings with the chassis; landing dust ring (`particles.ring`); boost: exhaust flame glows, a speed-line\noverlay, FOV kick, chevron flash; checkpoint: gate ring flash + `glints`; respawn: glints + scale-in; finish: confetti\n(`bits` in env colours), fireworks over the stands after a medal; splash at the mill pond; snow puffs off pine\nbranches when you pass close. Screen shake and flashes follow the engine's comfort settings.\n\n### 7.6 UI art (pixel sprites via `E.sprite`, `E.font`, `E.ui`)\n\nLogo: `E.font.title('CRACKMANIA', …, { scale: 4, colors: ['#fff6d0', '#ffd060', '#ff8a2a', '#c8402a'], depth: 3 })`\nwith animated crack lines (pen-free 2D `px.line` zig-zags growing across the letters, then a puff of asphalt bits).\nMedal icons B/S/G/A (16 px discs with ribbon and letter), copper coin, flag, lock, env emblems (cactus, cabbage,\nsnowflake), car silhouettes, chunky timer digits (9×14 px, outlined), **controller glyphs**: PlayStation (✕ ○ □ △ in\ntheir shapes and colours, L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, Create, sticks, d-pad), Xbox (A B X Y in coloured circles, LB RB LT\nRT, Menu, View), keyboard keycaps (letter or word), mouse (left/right/wheel). Panels: `E.ui.box` with a dark\ntranslucent gradient and the environment accent border.\n\n### 7.7 Animation list (everything that moves, built on the engine's rigs, tweens and scripts)\n\nCar: suspension, lean, wheel spin and steer, brake/head lights, boost flames, landing squash, flop roll-over, respawn\nscale-in, finish slow-motion. Camera: flyover intro, chase lag, FOV with speed, TV cuts, finish orbit. Characters:\nCoco's dialog gestures (pose changes per line among the engine's poses `wave`, `hips`, `cheer`, `cast`, plus\n`point: true` to point) and portrait expressions (`expr: 'smile' | 'shout'`), Drapeau's flag routine, the crowd, the podium cheer, Survival rivals' portraits reacting (smile when ahead,\nwince when beaten). World: windmills, pumpjack, cows, tumbleweeds, ski-lift, flags, start lights, flip boards,\nconfetti, fireworks. UI: tile focus scale, medal drop-in (outBack) and shine sweep, coppers count-up with coin ticks,\npalette slide, block drop-in with bounce in the editor and the attract build time-lapse, logo crack, unlock \"stamp\".\n\n---\n\n## 8. Audio, story and text","numLines":135,"startLine":975,"totalLines":1425}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YTinVGpZu6DerUysT2xsSX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
