{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SB3bixf4NgALfcGNT7f7jB","type":"tool_result","content":"1109\t## 8. Audio, story and text\n1110\t\n1111\t### 8.1 Music and sound (all synthesized; `game.audio` + `game.audio.ctx`)\n1112\t\n1113\tSongs in the engine's notation (`{ bpm, steps, tracks: [{ wave, vol, notes, name, on }] }`, drums `k s h o c t`),\n1114\tlooping, with **layers** (`audio.layer`) so intensity rises in play (drums and lead join after the first checkpoint;\n1115\teverything drops to bass + pad while paused via `duck`):\n1116\t\n1117\t| Song | Where | Feel |\n1118\t| --- | --- | --- |\n1119\t| Crack the Clock | title, menus, attract | upbeat electro-funk, 128 bpm, slap-bass triangle, square lead hook |\n1120\t| Heat Shimmer | Dustbowl races | desert surf-rock electro, 140 bpm, E minor pentatonic, twangy pulse12 lead |\n1121\t| Hedge Fund | Hedgerow races | bouncy Euro-house, 126 bpm, offbeat hats, major key |\n1122\t| Thin Ice | Frostpeak races | airy trance, 136 bpm, saw arpeggios, sine pad |\n1123\t| Blueprint | editor, puzzles | chill lo-fi, 96 bpm, soft triangle chords |\n1124\t| Ghost Guild | Survival | tense half-time drum & bass, 170 bpm |\n1125\t| Paint Job | garage, replays | jazzy chiptune, 110 bpm |\n1126\t| Victory Lap | credits, gauntlet cleared | anthem |\n1127\tStings (`audio.sting`): countdown (three low beeps, high GO), checkpoint chime (bright two-note up), new record\n1128\t(arpeggio), finish fanfare, medal stings (bronze 3 notes, silver 4, gold arpeggio + crash, author extended), unlock\n1129\tstamp, Survival elimination (descending wah), rank up.\n1130\t\n1131\t**Car sound** (`car/sound.js`, WebAudio nodes made once per car voice; volume follows `game.audio.volume ×\n1132\tsfxVolume`, silent when muted, paused or headless): engine = two detuned oscillators + a sub through a waveshaper and\n1133\tlowpass (Coyote: saw + sub, deep; Pebble: pulse/square, buzzy; Moose: saw + filtered noise, gravelly); a simulated\n1134\tgearbox — `gear = 1..5` from speed bands, `rpm = idle + (speed within band)·(redline − idle)`, a 60 ms dip and blip on\n1135\tshifts; throttle opens the filter. Tyres: band-passed noise ∝ slide, colour by surface (squeal / crunch / hiss / ice\n1136\twhine). Wind: low-passed noise ∝ speed². Scrape: noise while touching a wall. One-shots via `audio.sfx` voices: boost\n1137\twhoosh, landing thump (∝ impact), crash, respawn warp, horn (two-tone square toot + a babble \"beep beep\"), CP\n1138\tchime, gate whoosh-by, crowd cheer (noise swell + many tiny babbles), UI move/confirm/back/error, coin tick, block\n1139\tplace thunk / remove pop / rotate click / level blip, puzzle piece \"click-in\".\n1140\t\n1141\t### 8.2 Story beats and characters (`story/story.js`)\n1142\t\n1143\tDelivered with `E.Dialog` (portrait = the speaker's rig; typewriter text; each line voiced by babble §8.4; ✕/Enter/click\n1144\tadvances; ○ skips the scene). Lines are short. Beats fire once (recorded in the profile):\n1145\t\n1146\t| Beat | Trigger | Lines |\n1147\t| --- | --- | --- |\n1148\t| Welcome | first boot, after \"PRESS START\" | COCO: \"Bonjour! I am Coco Asphalte. I build tracks.\" / \"You drive them. Fast. Then faster.\" / \"Beat my clock and I pay you in coppers. Allez!\" |\n1149\t| Tips: D1 | first D1 run (non-modal radio-style lines at the right moments) | \"Hold {gas} to go. Steer with {steer}.\" / at the CP: \"Checkpoints remember you. {respawn} puts you back there.\" / after a respawn or 25 s: \"{restart} starts again. Nobody is watching. Except the clock.\" |\n1150\t| Tips: D2 | first kicker | \"Jumps need speed. The canyon does not negotiate.\" |\n1151\t| Tips: D3 | before the loop | \"Loops love speed. Keep your foot down.\" |\n1152\t| First medal | first medal ever | \"A medal! I knew you were not just a passenger.\" |\n1153\t| Puzzles open | event | \"I built a track and lost some pieces. Find a way from start to finish. The fastest way wins.\" |\n1154\t| Survival opens | event | TEX: \"Three ghosts. One road.\" / GRAVILLON: \"Finish last, go home.\" / BOBO: \"Hrrm. Bobo is hungry.\" |\n1155\t| Hedgerow opens | event | COCO: \"A farmer called. He wants a race track in his cabbage field. I said yes before he finished.\" |\n1156\t| Frostpeak opens | event | COCO: \"Next: the mountain. The asphalt is frozen. So am I. Allez!\" |\n1157\t| Editor first open | event | \"My toolbox. Every block costs coppers.\" / \"A track counts only once you drive it, start to finish.\" |\n1158\t| Environment cracked | golds on all 5 races of an env | \"You cracked {ENV}. I will need more asphalt.\" |\n1159\t| Ending | golds on all 15 | \"Fifteen tracks. Fifteen golds. The clock is crying in a corner.\" / \"Now build your own. I will be watching. With a stopwatch.\" → credits roll |\n1160\t\n1161\tResults quips (one per result, by medal; random from a small pool with `E.rng`): none — \"The clock wins this round.\n1162\tAgain?\" · Bronze — \"Bronze. The colour of honest effort.\" · Silver — \"Silver! Almost shiny enough.\" · Gold — \"Gold.\n1163\tCoco approves.\" · Author — \"You beat my own time. Rude. Magnificent.\" Survival: rank up — GRAVILLON \"Not bad. For a\n1164\tliving person.\"; BOBO \"Bobo likes you. Bobo still wins.\"; elimination — TEX \"Go home, rookie. Take the scenic route.\";\n1165\tgauntlet cleared — all three: \"...We will haunt you next season.\" Hot Seat card: COCO \"No peeking at the other times.\"\n1166\tBoot messages: \"Pouring asphalt\", \"Polishing medals\", \"Counting coppers\", \"Teaching cacti to wave\", \"Warming up the\n1167\tghosts\", \"Inflating the loops\", \"Hiding the cabbages\".\n1168\t\n1169\t### 8.3 Writing style (TrackMania 2003's)\n1170\t\n1171\tTrackMania's text is sparse, functional and a little cheeky: menu words, track names, medal messages, almost no\n1172\tstory. Keep that: **UI labels are one or two words in capitals** (RACE, PUZZLE, SURVIVAL, BUILD, MULTIPLAYER, GARAGE,\n1173\tREPLAYS, OPTIONS, ABOUT; RETRY, NEXT, VALIDATE). **Host lines are at most ~60 characters**, one joke at most, dry, never\n1174\tmean; a French word now and then (Bonjour, Allez, Voilà, Bof) for Coco only. Track names are two or three words with a\n1175\tpun or a place (Sunburn Strip, Hay Fever, Yeti Summit). Prompts are verbs (`✕ DRIVE`, `○ BACK`). All strings live in\n1176\t`data/text.js` with `{gas}`-style placeholders filled from `game.input.label()`.\n1177\t\n1178\t### 8.4 Gibberish voices (`audio/babble.js`)\n1179\t\n1180\tAnimalese-style: each letter of the line is one syllable (55–75 ms by speaker speed). Vowels pick formants (a 800/1200\n1181\tHz, e 400/2000, i 300/2300, o 450/800, u 325/700) as two band-pass filters (Q≈6) over the speaker's oscillator;\n1182\tconsonants add a 12–18 ms tick (fricatives s f h z: high-passed noise; plosives b d g k p t: a click); pitch = speaker\n1183\tbase × (1 + 0.15·hash(letter)), rising on \"?\", falling on \".\" and \"!\"-boosted; pauses: comma 120 ms, full stop 220 ms;\n1184\tspaces 40 ms. Speakers: Coco (triangle, 330 Hz, quick), Drapeau (square, 200 Hz), Tex (pulse12, 240 Hz, nasal Q 9),\n1185\tGravillon (sine + triangle, 300 Hz, clipped), Bobo (saw, 120 Hz, slow, growly), crowd (many random short babbles,\n1186\trandom pitches, low volume). The dialog typewriter reveals one letter per syllable so mouths and text stay in sync.\n1187\tHeadless: no-op. Honour mute/volume.\n1188\t\n1189\t---\n1190\t\n1191\t## 9. Testing\n1192\t\n1193\t### 9.1 Headless loader (validated while planning: three r182 and Rapier load and step in Node 24)\n1194\t\n1195\t```js\n1196\t// tools/node-env.mjs — the engine, the 3D engine and the game in Node, no browser\n1197\timport { registerHooks } from 'node:module';\n1198\timport { pathToFileURL, fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n1199\timport vm from 'node:vm';\n1200\timport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1201\tconst ROOT = fileURLToPath(new URL('..', import.meta.url)), V = ROOT + 'engine/vendor/';\n1202\tconst MAP = { 'three': 'three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js', 'three/webgpu': 'three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js',\n1203\t  'three/tsl': 'three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js', '@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat': 'rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js' };\n1204\tregisterHooks({ resolve: (spec, ctx, next) => MAP[spec] ? { url: pathToFileURL(V + MAP[spec]).href, format: 'module', shortCircuit: true } : next(spec, ctx) });\n1205\tvm.runInThisContext(readFileSync(ROOT + 'engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'utf8'), { filename: 'my-3d2dge.js' });  // globalThis.My3D2dge\n1206\texport const E = globalThis.My3D2dge;\n1207\t// World3D bakes textures on canvases: hand it the 2D engine's headless stand-in canvas\n1208\tconst standIn = () => { const d = globalThis.document; delete globalThis.document; const c = E.mkCanvas(1, 1); globalThis.document = d; return c; };\n1209\tglobalThis.document = { createElement: standIn, getElementById: () => null, querySelector: () => null, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {} };\n1210\tawait import(pathToFileURL(ROOT + 'engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js').href);                                   // E.World3D, E.THREE, E.RAPIER\n1211\texport async function makeGame(o = {}) {\n1212\t  const { createGame } = await import(pathToFileURL(ROOT + 'src/main.js').href);\n1213\t  const g = await createGame({ headless: true, ...o }); await g.game.booted; return g;                 // { game, api }\n1214\t}\n1215\t```\n1216\tIn Node, `new E.Game({ headless: true })` has no screen and skips `draw`; `E.World3D.init(game)` returns after\n1217\t`RAPIER.init()` without a renderer; worlds build their meshes but never render. Rapier prints a harmless \"deprecated\n1218\tparameters\" warning on init — filter it from test output."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"03d332e8-fc82-42f5-a5a7-0ff975075856","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:40:19.006Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 8. Audio, story and text\n\n### 8.1 Music and sound (all synthesized; `game.audio` + `game.audio.ctx`)\n\nSongs in the engine's notation (`{ bpm, steps, tracks: [{ wave, vol, notes, name, on }] }`, drums `k s h o c t`),\nlooping, with **layers** (`audio.layer`) so intensity rises in play (drums and lead join after the first checkpoint;\neverything drops to bass + pad while paused via `duck`):\n\n| Song | Where | Feel |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Crack the Clock | title, menus, attract | upbeat electro-funk, 128 bpm, slap-bass triangle, square lead hook |\n| Heat Shimmer | Dustbowl races | desert surf-rock electro, 140 bpm, E minor pentatonic, twangy pulse12 lead |\n| Hedge Fund | Hedgerow races | bouncy Euro-house, 126 bpm, offbeat hats, major key |\n| Thin Ice | Frostpeak races | airy trance, 136 bpm, saw arpeggios, sine pad |\n| Blueprint | editor, puzzles | chill lo-fi, 96 bpm, soft triangle chords |\n| Ghost Guild | Survival | tense half-time drum & bass, 170 bpm |\n| Paint Job | garage, replays | jazzy chiptune, 110 bpm |\n| Victory Lap | credits, gauntlet cleared | anthem |\nStings (`audio.sting`): countdown (three low beeps, high GO), checkpoint chime (bright two-note up), new record\n(arpeggio), finish fanfare, medal stings (bronze 3 notes, silver 4, gold arpeggio + crash, author extended), unlock\nstamp, Survival elimination (descending wah), rank up.\n\n**Car sound** (`car/sound.js`, WebAudio nodes made once per car voice; volume follows `game.audio.volume ×\nsfxVolume`, silent when muted, paused or headless): engine = two detuned oscillators + a sub through a waveshaper and\nlowpass (Coyote: saw + sub, deep; Pebble: pulse/square, buzzy; Moose: saw + filtered noise, gravelly); a simulated\ngearbox — `gear = 1..5` from speed bands, `rpm = idle + (speed within band)·(redline − idle)`, a 60 ms dip and blip on\nshifts; throttle opens the filter. Tyres: band-passed noise ∝ slide, colour by surface (squeal / crunch / hiss / ice\nwhine). Wind: low-passed noise ∝ speed². Scrape: noise while touching a wall. One-shots via `audio.sfx` voices: boost\nwhoosh, landing thump (∝ impact), crash, respawn warp, horn (two-tone square toot + a babble \"beep beep\"), CP\nchime, gate whoosh-by, crowd cheer (noise swell + many tiny babbles), UI move/confirm/back/error, coin tick, block\nplace thunk / remove pop / rotate click / level blip, puzzle piece \"click-in\".\n\n### 8.2 Story beats and characters (`story/story.js`)\n\nDelivered with `E.Dialog` (portrait = the speaker's rig; typewriter text; each line voiced by babble §8.4; ✕/Enter/click\nadvances; ○ skips the scene). Lines are short. Beats fire once (recorded in the profile):\n\n| Beat | Trigger | Lines |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Welcome | first boot, after \"PRESS START\" | COCO: \"Bonjour! I am Coco Asphalte. I build tracks.\" / \"You drive them. Fast. Then faster.\" / \"Beat my clock and I pay you in coppers. Allez!\" |\n| Tips: D1 | first D1 run (non-modal radio-style lines at the right moments) | \"Hold {gas} to go. Steer with {steer}.\" / at the CP: \"Checkpoints remember you. {respawn} puts you back there.\" / after a respawn or 25 s: \"{restart} starts again. Nobody is watching. Except the clock.\" |\n| Tips: D2 | first kicker | \"Jumps need speed. The canyon does not negotiate.\" |\n| Tips: D3 | before the loop | \"Loops love speed. Keep your foot down.\" |\n| First medal | first medal ever | \"A medal! I knew you were not just a passenger.\" |\n| Puzzles open | event | \"I built a track and lost some pieces. Find a way from start to finish. The fastest way wins.\" |\n| Survival opens | event | TEX: \"Three ghosts. One road.\" / GRAVILLON: \"Finish last, go home.\" / BOBO: \"Hrrm. Bobo is hungry.\" |\n| Hedgerow opens | event | COCO: \"A farmer called. He wants a race track in his cabbage field. I said yes before he finished.\" |\n| Frostpeak opens | event | COCO: \"Next: the mountain. The asphalt is frozen. So am I. Allez!\" |\n| Editor first open | event | \"My toolbox. Every block costs coppers.\" / \"A track counts only once you drive it, start to finish.\" |\n| Environment cracked | golds on all 5 races of an env | \"You cracked {ENV}. I will need more asphalt.\" |\n| Ending | golds on all 15 | \"Fifteen tracks. Fifteen golds. The clock is crying in a corner.\" / \"Now build your own. I will be watching. With a stopwatch.\" → credits roll |\n\nResults quips (one per result, by medal; random from a small pool with `E.rng`): none — \"The clock wins this round.\nAgain?\" · Bronze — \"Bronze. The colour of honest effort.\" · Silver — \"Silver! Almost shiny enough.\" · Gold — \"Gold.\nCoco approves.\" · Author — \"You beat my own time. Rude. Magnificent.\" Survival: rank up — GRAVILLON \"Not bad. For a\nliving person.\"; BOBO \"Bobo likes you. Bobo still wins.\"; elimination — TEX \"Go home, rookie. Take the scenic route.\";\ngauntlet cleared — all three: \"...We will haunt you next season.\" Hot Seat card: COCO \"No peeking at the other times.\"\nBoot messages: \"Pouring asphalt\", \"Polishing medals\", \"Counting coppers\", \"Teaching cacti to wave\", \"Warming up the\nghosts\", \"Inflating the loops\", \"Hiding the cabbages\".\n\n### 8.3 Writing style (TrackMania 2003's)\n\nTrackMania's text is sparse, functional and a little cheeky: menu words, track names, medal messages, almost no\nstory. Keep that: **UI labels are one or two words in capitals** (RACE, PUZZLE, SURVIVAL, BUILD, MULTIPLAYER, GARAGE,\nREPLAYS, OPTIONS, ABOUT; RETRY, NEXT, VALIDATE). **Host lines are at most ~60 characters**, one joke at most, dry, never\nmean; a French word now and then (Bonjour, Allez, Voilà, Bof) for Coco only. Track names are two or three words with a\npun or a place (Sunburn Strip, Hay Fever, Yeti Summit). Prompts are verbs (`✕ DRIVE`, `○ BACK`). All strings live in\n`data/text.js` with `{gas}`-style placeholders filled from `game.input.label()`.\n\n### 8.4 Gibberish voices (`audio/babble.js`)\n\nAnimalese-style: each letter of the line is one syllable (55–75 ms by speaker speed). Vowels pick formants (a 800/1200\nHz, e 400/2000, i 300/2300, o 450/800, u 325/700) as two band-pass filters (Q≈6) over the speaker's oscillator;\nconsonants add a 12–18 ms tick (fricatives s f h z: high-passed noise; plosives b d g k p t: a click); pitch = speaker\nbase × (1 + 0.15·hash(letter)), rising on \"?\", falling on \".\" and \"!\"-boosted; pauses: comma 120 ms, full stop 220 ms;\nspaces 40 ms. Speakers: Coco (triangle, 330 Hz, quick), Drapeau (square, 200 Hz), Tex (pulse12, 240 Hz, nasal Q 9),\nGravillon (sine + triangle, 300 Hz, clipped), Bobo (saw, 120 Hz, slow, growly), crowd (many random short babbles,\nrandom pitches, low volume). The dialog typewriter reveals one letter per syllable so mouths and text stay in sync.\nHeadless: no-op. Honour mute/volume.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Testing\n\n### 9.1 Headless loader (validated while planning: three r182 and Rapier load and step in Node 24)\n\n```js\n// tools/node-env.mjs — the engine, the 3D engine and the game in Node, no browser\nimport { registerHooks } from 'node:module';\nimport { pathToFileURL, fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nconst ROOT = fileURLToPath(new URL('..', import.meta.url)), V = ROOT + 'engine/vendor/';\nconst MAP = { 'three': 'three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js', 'three/webgpu': 'three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js',\n  'three/tsl': 'three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js', '@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat': 'rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js' };\nregisterHooks({ resolve: (spec, ctx, next) => MAP[spec] ? { url: pathToFileURL(V + MAP[spec]).href, format: 'module', shortCircuit: true } : next(spec, ctx) });\nvm.runInThisContext(readFileSync(ROOT + 'engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'utf8'), { filename: 'my-3d2dge.js' });  // globalThis.My3D2dge\nexport const E = globalThis.My3D2dge;\n// World3D bakes textures on canvases: hand it the 2D engine's headless stand-in canvas\nconst standIn = () => { const d = globalThis.document; delete globalThis.document; const c = E.mkCanvas(1, 1); globalThis.document = d; return c; };\nglobalThis.document = { createElement: standIn, getElementById: () => null, querySelector: () => null, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {} };\nawait import(pathToFileURL(ROOT + 'engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js').href);                                   // E.World3D, E.THREE, E.RAPIER\nexport async function makeGame(o = {}) {\n  const { createGame } = await import(pathToFileURL(ROOT + 'src/main.js').href);\n  const g = await createGame({ headless: true, ...o }); await g.game.booted; return g;                 // { game, api }\n}\n```\nIn Node, `new E.Game({ headless: true })` has no screen and skips `draw`; `E.World3D.init(game)` returns after\n`RAPIER.init()` without a renderer; worlds build their meshes but never render. Rapier prints a harmless \"deprecated\nparameters\" warning on init — filter it from test output.","numLines":110,"startLine":1109,"totalLines":1425}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SB3bixf4NgALfcGNT7f7jB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
