{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3MGh6uzoxk14CtYJVi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Throttle now fails at 40 km/h and holds from about 47, and coasting fails at 101 and holds from about 107. I'm updating §4.4, §2.1, Appendix B and the §9.3 physics checks to these measured figures.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1300,"cache_read_input_tokens":570649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1300},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"0f44f1b3-0b41-4f17-b1f6-d1080ee46112","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:44:41.934Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3MGRENwL2FqEdCAK7e","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3MGh6uzoxk14CtYJVi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TpvbbVJXFnSN7czgbdKvNX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, ('MISSING' if s.count(a) == 0 else 'MULTI', a[:80])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n# §2.1 claim\nrep(\"\"\"**kinematic surface-following arcade model** that was prototyped and validated headless for this plan (§4.4): it\nholds a 12 m loop at ~110 km/h entry (≈80 km/h at the top), exits upright, launches off a kicker (2.4 s airtime) and\nlands cleanly.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**kinematic surface-following arcade model** that was prototyped and validated headless for this plan (§4.4,\nAppendix A): with the Coyote's tuning it holds a 12 m loop on full throttle from ~47 km/h entry (coasting needs ~107),\ndrops off the top below that, and clears a two-cell gap from a 15° kicker at ≥ ~150 km/h, landing upright.\"\"\")\n# §4.4 contact\nrep(\"\"\"       holds = pull <= (|v|² − vn²)·car.kappa + A              A = CFG.adhesion (0.35 g)\n       car.slip = holds ? 0 : car.slip + dt\"\"\",\n\"\"\"       vt2 = |v|² − vn²;  Aeff = A·min(1, sqrt(vt2) / 15 m/s)   A = CFG.adhesion (0.35 g), fading out at low speed\n       load = vt2·car.kappa − pull + Aeff                         (normal load per unit mass; ≥ 0: the surface holds you)\n       car.slip = load >= 0 ? 0 : car.slip + dt\"\"\")\n# §4.4 grounded: traction\nrep(\"\"\"     a = g − n(g·n)                                               (gravity along the surface: slopes matter)\n     gas:   if s < vtop: a += f·gas·A0·(1 − (max(s,0)/vtop)^1.6)\n     brake: if s > 0.5 m/s: a −= v̂·brake·B (clamp so v doesn't reverse this step)\n            else: a −= f·brake·Arev while s > −vrev           (reverse)\"\"\",\n\"\"\"     a = g − n(g·n)                                               (gravity along the surface: slopes matter)\n     traction = surface.grip·max(0, load)                         (what the tyres can pass on: μ·N/m)\n     gas:   if s < vtop: a += f·min(traction, gas·A0·(1 − (max(s,0)/vtop)^1.6))\n     brake: if s > 0.5 m/s: a −= v̂·min(traction, brake·B) (clamp so v doesn't reverse this step)\n            else: a −= f·min(traction, brake·Arev) while s > −vrev   (reverse)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"     grip: vlat = v·r; maxDv = grip·surface.grip·(drift ? driftGrip : 1)·dt\"\"\",\n\"\"\"     grip: vlat = v·r; maxDv = grip·surface.grip·(load/G)·(drift ? driftGrip : 1)·dt   (= the tuned grip on flat\n           ground; more when pressed into a loop or bank, less over a crest or upside down)\"\"\")\n# §4.4 prototype result paragraph\nrep(\"\"\"Prototype result (headless, Rapier 0.19.3 trimesh ribbons, G = 1.6 g, adhesion 0.35 g, ride 0.55 m, reach 0.9 m):\nentering a 12 m-radius loop at 110 km/h, the car stayed grounded the whole way (≈ 80 km/h at the top, up = −0.99) and\nleft it upright; a 20° kicker at ~110 km/h gave 2.4 s of air and an upright landing 50 m later. With averaged triangle\nnormals instead of the four-point plane, the car detached on every flat facet — keep the plane fit. Without lane\nassist, a loop whose exit is shifted sideways throws the car off its side — keep the assist on loop blocks.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Prototype results (headless, Rapier 0.19.3 trimesh ribbons, Appendix A's code exactly as printed: Coyote tuning,\nG = 1.5 g, adhesion 0.35 g, ride 0.55 m, reach 0.9 m): **12 m loop on full throttle** — 40 km/h entry drops off the\ntop, 47 km/h holds (46 km/h over the top), 59–102 km/h hold; **coasting** — 101 km/h drops off, 107 km/h holds;\n**15° kicker, 64 m gap, landing pad from +3 m** — 135 km/h at the lip falls into the gap, 161 / 181 / 194 km/h land\nupright 9 / 29 / 45 m into the pad after 1.65–2.07 s of air. Two lessons from the spike: averaging triangle normals\ninstead of the four-point plane made the car let go on every flat facet of the loop (keep the plane fit); without\ntraction limits the engine pushed the car up the loop from any speed (keep `traction`). In a full-course run with a\nsideways-shifted loop (as the loop block has), the car stayed on only with lane assist — keep it on loop blocks.\"\"\")\n# §9.3 physics checks\nrep(\"\"\"**loop at 120 km/h entry: grounded all the way, exits upright**; loop at 55 km/h: detaches before the top and falls;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**loop block on full throttle from ≥ 60 km/h: grounded all the way, exits upright; from ≤ 40 km/h: detaches at\nthe top; coasting from ≥ 115 km/h holds, ≤ 95 km/h fails** (re-measure and update these numbers if tuning changes);\nice: acceleration capped by traction (≤ 0.35 × asphalt's from standstill);\"\"\")\n# Appendix B row\nrep(\"\"\"| The car model holds loops and lands jumps | Appendix A in Node with Rapier trimesh ribbons: 12 m loop at 110 km/h entry held throughout (≈ 80 km/h at the top), exited upright; kicker → 2.4 s air → upright landing |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| The car model holds loops and lands jumps | Appendix A, extracted from this file and run in Node with Rapier trimesh ribbons: loop thresholds and kicker landings as listed under §4.4 \"Prototype results\" |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"## Appendix A — the validated car core (reference code from the planning spike)\n\nEngine units (`U = 16` per metre), z up, `dt = 1/120`. `pw` is TrackPhysics' Rapier world (fixed trimesh colliders\nonly). This is the code that held the loop and landed the jump; §4.4 adds steering, grip limits, surfaces, boost,\nwalls, flop and lane assist on top of it. Vectors are `[x, y, z]` arrays.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"## Appendix A — the validated car core (reference code from the planning spike)\n\nEngine units (`U = 16` per metre), z up, `dt = 1/120`. `pw` is TrackPhysics' Rapier world (fixed trimesh colliders\nonly), `RAPIER` the module (`E.RAPIER`). This exact code produced §4.4's prototype results; §4.4 adds steering, the\ngrip/drift model, surfaces, boost, walls, flop, landing loss and lane assist on top of it. Vectors are `[x, y, z]`\narrays.\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF","description":"Update car model text, claims and tests with measured thresholds"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1300,"cache_read_input_tokens":570649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1300},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"737c0f30-c191-4afb-b043-326909480c76","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:45:01.143Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3MGRENwL2FqEdCAK7e","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TpvbbVJXFnSN7czgbdKvNX":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, ('MISSING' if s.count(a) == 0 else 'MULTI', a[:80])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n# §2.1 claim\nrep(\"\"\"**kinematic surface-following arcade model** that was prototyped and validated headless for this plan (§4.4): it\nholds a 12 m loop at ~110 km/h entry (≈80 km/h at the top), exits upright, launches off a kicker (2.4 s airtime) and\nlands cleanly.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**kinematic surface-following arcade model** that was prototyped and validated headless for this plan (§4.4,\nAppendix A): with the Coyote's tuning it holds a 12 m loop on full throttle from ~47 km/h entry (coasting needs ~107),\ndrops off the top below that, and clears a two-cell gap from a 15° kicker at ≥ ~150 km/h, landing upright.\"\"\")\n# §4.4 contact\nrep(\"\"\"       holds = pull <= (|v|² − vn²)·car.kappa + A              A = CFG.adhesion (0.35 g)\n       car.slip = holds ? 0 : car.slip + dt\"\"\",\n\"\"\"       vt2 = |v|² − vn²;  Aeff = A·min(1, sqrt(vt2) / 15 m/s)   A = CFG.adhesion (0.35 g), fading out at low speed\n       load = vt2·car.kappa − pull + Aeff                         (normal load per unit mass; ≥ 0: the surface holds you)\n       car.slip = load >= 0 ? 0 : car.slip + dt\"\"\")\n# §4.4 grounded: traction\nrep(\"\"\"     a = g − n(g·n)                                               (gravity along the surface: slopes matter)\n     gas:   if s < vtop: a += f·gas·A0·(1 − (max(s,0)/vtop)^1.6)\n     brake: if s > 0.5 m/s: a −= v̂·brake·B (clamp so v doesn't reverse this step)\n            else: a −= f·brake·Arev while s > −vrev           (reverse)\"\"\",\n\"\"\"     a = g − n(g·n)                                               (gravity along the surface: slopes matter)\n     traction = surface.grip·max(0, load)                         (what the tyres can pass on: μ·N/m)\n     gas:   if s < vtop: a += f·min(traction, gas·A0·(1 − (max(s,0)/vtop)^1.6))\n     brake: if s > 0.5 m/s: a −= v̂·min(traction, brake·B) (clamp so v doesn't reverse this step)\n            else: a −= f·min(traction, brake·Arev) while s > −vrev   (reverse)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"     grip: vlat = v·r; maxDv = grip·surface.grip·(drift ? driftGrip : 1)·dt\"\"\",\n\"\"\"     grip: vlat = v·r; maxDv = grip·surface.grip·(load/G)·(drift ? driftGrip : 1)·dt   (= the tuned grip on flat\n           ground; more when pressed into a loop or bank, less over a crest or upside down)\"\"\")\n# §4.4 prototype result paragraph\nrep(\"\"\"Prototype result (headless, Rapier 0.19.3 trimesh ribbons, G = 1.6 g, adhesion 0.35 g, ride 0.55 m, reach 0.9 m):\nentering a 12 m-radius loop at 110 km/h, the car stayed grounded the whole way (≈ 80 km/h at the top, up = −0.99) and\nleft it upright; a 20° kicker at ~110 km/h gave 2.4 s of air and an upright landing 50 m later. With averaged triangle\nnormals instead of the four-point plane, the car detached on every flat facet — keep the plane fit. Without lane\nassist, a loop whose exit is shifted sideways throws the car off its side — keep the assist on loop blocks.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Prototype results (headless, Rapier 0.19.3 trimesh ribbons, Appendix A's code exactly as printed: Coyote tuning,\nG = 1.5 g, adhesion 0.35 g, ride 0.55 m, reach 0.9 m): **12 m loop on full throttle** — 40 km/h entry drops off the\ntop, 47 km/h holds (46 km/h over the top), 59–102 km/h hold; **coasting** — 101 km/h drops off, 107 km/h holds;\n**15° kicker, 64 m gap, landing pad from +3 m** — 135 km/h at the lip falls into the gap, 161 / 181 / 194 km/h land\nupright 9 / 29 / 45 m into the pad after 1.65–2.07 s of air. Two lessons from the spike: averaging triangle normals\ninstead of the four-point plane made the car let go on every flat facet of the loop (keep the plane fit); without\ntraction limits the engine pushed the car up the loop from any speed (keep `traction`). In a full-course run with a\nsideways-shifted loop (as the loop block has), the car stayed on only with lane assist — keep it on loop blocks.\"\"\")\n# §9.3 physics checks\nrep(\"\"\"**loop at 120 km/h entry: grounded all the way, exits upright**; loop at 55 km/h: detaches before the top and falls;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**loop block on full throttle from ≥ 60 km/h: grounded all the way, exits upright; from ≤ 40 km/h: detaches at\nthe top; coasting from ≥ 115 km/h holds, ≤ 95 km/h fails** (re-measure and update these numbers if tuning changes);\nice: acceleration capped by traction (≤ 0.35 × asphalt's from standstill);\"\"\")\n# Appendix B row\nrep(\"\"\"| The car model holds loops and lands jumps | Appendix A in Node with Rapier trimesh ribbons: 12 m loop at 110 km/h entry held throughout (≈ 80 km/h at the top), exited upright; kicker → 2.4 s air → upright landing |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| The car model holds loops and lands jumps | Appendix A, extracted from this file and run in Node with Rapier trimesh ribbons: loop thresholds and kicker landings as listed under §4.4 \"Prototype results\" |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"## Appendix A — the validated car core (reference code from the planning spike)\n\nEngine units (`U = 16` per metre), z up, `dt = 1/120`. `pw` is TrackPhysics' Rapier world (fixed trimesh colliders\nonly). This is the code that held the loop and landed the jump; §4.4 adds steering, grip limits, surfaces, boost,\nwalls, flop and lane assist on top of it. Vectors are `[x, y, z]` arrays.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"## Appendix A — the validated car core (reference code from the planning spike)\n\nEngine units (`U = 16` per metre), z up, `dt = 1/120`. `pw` is TrackPhysics' Rapier world (fixed trimesh colliders\nonly), `RAPIER` the module (`E.RAPIER`). This exact code produced §4.4's prototype results; §4.4 adds steering, the\ngrip/drift model, surfaces, boost, walls, flop, landing loss and lane assist on top of it. Vectors are `[x, y, z]`\narrays.\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF","description":"Update car model text, claims and tests with measured thresholds"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01TpvbbVJXFnSN7czgbdKvNX":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work"}}}
