{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VdiDRyaViYBzMGo8rjFU9E","type":"tool_result","content":"1230:prints **only** `FAIL <suite>: <check>: <detail>` lines and one summary line (`247 checks, 0 failed, 12.4 s`); exit\n1246:| `physics` | (Coyote unless noted) 0→100 km/h in 2.6–3.6 s; reaches ≥ 97% vtop on a long straight; 100→0 braking in 12–22 m; R2 at 110 km/h holds the lane, R1 at 110 km/h runs wide (needs braking); **loop block on full throttle from ≥ 60 km/h: grounded all the way, exits upright; from ≤ 40 km/h: detaches at\n125:engine/assets/                      <- dist/handoff/src/assets/sets/<set>.js (only the sets you load; see §7.4)\n137:  converted once when loaded (`U = 16`).\n229:    node-env.mjs        headless loader (§9.1: import hooks + document stub + engine load)\n246:  2 'Reading your profile'      profile.load()\n253:  6 'Teaching cacti to wave'    title showcase: load D3 into Dustbowl, start the demo bot (cheat mode)\n283:   loading the 2D engine in Node), `<div id=\"stage\"><canvas id=\"view\"></canvas><canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas></div>`,\n496:       load = vt2·car.kappa − pull + Aeff                         (normal load per unit mass; ≥ 0: the surface holds you)\n497:       car.slip = load >= 0 ? 0 : car.slip + dt\n508:     traction = surface.grip·max(0, load)                         (what the tyres can pass on: μ·N/m)\n519:     grip: vlat = v·r; maxDv = grip·surface.grip·(load/G)·(drift ? driftGrip : 1)·dt   (= the tuned grip on flat\n807:   pick on every copy; the seed changes per round, so rounds rotate tracks); load it.\n1200:### 9.1 Headless loader (validated while planning: three r182 and Rapier load and step in Node 24)\n1229:`node tools/test.mjs [suite ...] [--browser] [--hub] [--all]` loads the engine once, runs the suites in-process, and\n1233:`input.hold/tap/press`, `game.debug.snapshot()` and the `api` handle (load track, place car, run bot, editor\n1252:| `campaign` | unlock rules (D1–D2 open; next on medal; puzzles/survival/env gates); coppers ledger (rewards, block costs, refunds, packs, patterns); story beats fire once; profile save/load/migrate |\n1253:| `editor` | place/rotate/raise/remove with occupancy and costs; refuse overlaps, out-of-grid, unaffordable; kicker reserves its gap; undo/redo 50 random ops returns to the same state and coppers; validate (bot drive) sets author + medals; any edit clears validation; save/load slots; share code round trip; export-as-content output compiles |\n1260:| `playthrough` | **the whole game, scripted**: fresh profile → welcome beat → all 15 races driven by the bot as the player through the real menus (pressing the real buttons) → medals, coppers and unlocks as designed → the 6 puzzles solved through the editor UI → each gauntlet run (bot at skill 1 clears it) → build and validate a 12-block track in the editor, save, reload, share code → paint a car in the garage → save and reopen a replay → hot seat (2 players) and split screen (2 players) races → golds everywhere → ending beat and credits → final profile matches expectations; 0 engine errors |\n1322:| Headless testing of a 3D engine | The loader in §9.1 was run successfully during planning; keep pure logic (track model, CarSim, run, bot, economy, editor ops) free of three.js calls so most suites don't depend on rendering at all |\n1328:| Shader stalls on track load / editing | All materials and pen batches (incl. ghost) made at boot; `world.prepare()`; only geometry changes later; dispose old geometries |\n1400:    c.load = vt2 * c.kappa - pull + aEff;                                   // normal load per unit mass","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800","uuid":"4b310c28-edeb-4d0f-976a-bb42b9ecf385","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:45:04.783Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1230:prints **only** `FAIL <suite>: <check>: <detail>` lines and one summary line (`247 checks, 0 failed, 12.4 s`); exit\n1246:| `physics`